{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012miaKH6NB6qHXBZJaUKpWJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'LLaMA replication失败彻底否定跨模型泛化性。Confusability signal被重新定位为Qwen3特有的schema敏感性模式，\n2\t  而非LLM通用属性。SDGD v2同样失败，确认merge amplification是decompose-and-merge范式的根本瓶颈， 而非embedding质量问题。论文转型为方法论框架：(1)\n3\t  multi-channel degradation作为诊断工具， (2) 2×3 embedding ablation + 跨模型分歧揭示one-size-fits-all\n4\t  decomposition注定失败， (3) centrality confound + merge amplification作为对该领域的警示性结果。 完全放弃SDGD作为method\n5\t  contribution；以\"negative results that reframe assumptions\"定位冲EMNLP Main， Findings作为fallback。\n6\t\n7\t  '\n8\timagined_experiments:\n9\t- name: DocRED Confusability Study\n10\t  plan_id: exp-005\n11\t  description: DocRED 96 relation types上的count curve + BCS correlation，跨任务(NER→RE\n12\t    document-level)压力测试\n13\t  expected_results:\n14\t    count_curve:\n15\t      count_1_acc: 0.72\n16\t      count_8_acc: 0.58\n17\t      count_16_acc: 0.49\n18\t      count_32_acc: 0.41\n19\t      count_64_acc: 0.33\n20\t      count_96_acc: 0.28\n21\t      degradation_pp: -44.0\n22\t    bcs_controlled:\n23\t      count_8_low_bcs_acc: 0.6\n24\t      count_8_high_bcs_acc: 0.55\n25\t      count_8_delta_pp: -5.0\n26\t      count_16_low_bcs_acc: 0.51\n27\t      count_16_high_bcs_acc: 0.47\n28\t      count_16_delta_pp: -4.0\n29\t    pairwise:\n30\t      pearson_r: 0.038\n31\t      pearson_p: 0.082\n32\t      n_pairs: 4560\n33\t      spearman_rho: 0.041\n34\t      spearman_p: 0.065\n35\t    per_type:\n36\t      spearman_rho: -0.07\n37\t      spearman_p: 0.52\n38\t      n_types: 80\n39\t  result_rationale: 'DocRED是document-level RE，每个instance涉及多句推理，relation extraction依赖于entity\n40\t    pair的跨句共指和推理链， 而非单句内的type assignment。这意味着extraction失败的主因是推理链断裂和entity pair识别错误，\n41\t    不是type confusion。高BCS type pairs（如\"capital_of\"与\"headquarters_location\"）在document\n42\t    context下 有充足的disambiguating evidence（地理实体 vs 组织实体），使embedding-based confusability不再是有效预测器。\n43\t    Count curve仍然work（attention dilution是universal的），但BCS controlled delta仅~4-5pp（噪声级），\n44\t    pairwise r在0.05门槛以上勉强不显著。这进一步削弱confusability作为跨任务通用信号的claim。\n45\t\n46\t    '\n47\t  tables:\n48\t  - name: 'Table: DocRED Count Curve'\n49\t    columns:\n50\t    - count\n51\t    - acc\n52\t    - bcs_mean\n53\t    - n_batches\n54\t    rows:\n55\t    - - 1\n56\t      - 0.72\n57\t      - 0.0\n58\t      - 96\n59\t    - - 8\n60\t      - 0.58\n61\t      - 0.68\n62\t      - 5\n63\t    - - 16\n64\t      - 0.49\n65\t      - 0.76\n66\t      - 5\n67\t    - - 32\n68\t      - 0.41\n69\t      - 0.85\n70\t      - 5\n71\t    - - 64\n72\t      - 0.33\n73\t      - 0.92\n74\t      - 5\n75\t    - - 96\n76\t      - 0.28\n77\t      - 0.97\n78\t      - 5\n79\t  - name: 'Table: DocRED BCS-Controlled'\n80\t    columns:\n81\t    - count\n82\t    - low_bcs_acc\n83\t    - high_bcs_acc\n84\t    - delta_pp\n85\t    rows:\n86\t    - - 8\n87\t      - 0.6\n88\t      - 0.55\n89\t      - -5.0\n90\t    - - 16\n91\t      - 0.51\n92\t      - 0.47\n93\t      - -4.0\n94\t  figures_description:\n95\t  - 'Count curve: 强降速曲线(0.72→0.28)，与FewRel 80-rel类似形态但更陡(document-level更难)'\n96\t  - 'BCS scatter: pairwise r=0.038，几乎平坦的regression line，数据点高度分散'\n97\t  - 'BCS-controlled bar chart: delta仅4-5pp，error bar重叠严重'\n98\t  analysis: 'DocRED count curve confirms universal count-degradation channel但confusability\n99\t    channel几乎消失。 Document-level RE中type confusion被cross-sentence reasoning failure淹没。\n100\t    在worst叙事下，这作为\"confusability signal是task-specific而非universal\"的额外证据， 进一步限制Claim\n101\t    1的generalizability scope到sentence-level NER/ED。 对论文的影响：如果做了DocRED，结果会被放入discussion\n102\t    section作为boundary condition， 但在worst tier下建议不执行此实验以避免浪费GPU时间——不在paper scope内。\n103\t\n104\t    '\n105\t- name: Count × Confusability Interaction Effect\n106\t  plan_id: exp-006\n107\t  description: 'Few-NERD上的2×2 factorial: {low count=6, high count=22} × {low BCS,\n108\t    high BCS}，检验additive vs multiplicative interaction'\n109\t  expected_results:\n110\t    cell_f1:\n111\t      low_count_low_bcs: 0.342\n112\t      low_count_high_bcs: 0.298\n113\t      high_count_low_bcs: 0.285\n114\t      high_count_high_bcs: 0.258\n115\t    main_effects:\n116\t      count_effect_pp: -4.9\n117\t      bcs_effect_pp: -3.6\n118\t    interaction:\n119\t      interaction_f: 0.42\n120\t      interaction_p: 0.52\n121\t      effect_type: sub-additive, non-significant\n122\t    simple_effects:\n123\t      bcs_effect_at_low_count_pp: -4.4\n124\t      bcs_effect_at_high_count_pp: -2.7\n125\t  result_rationale: '在worst tier下，interaction term不显著(p=0.52)表明count和confusability的交互模式模糊。\n126\t    简单效应分析显示BCS effect在high count下反而更小(-2.7pp vs -4.4pp at low count)， 这是因为high count下overall\n127\t    performance已经很低（floor effect）， confusability的额外degradation被压缩。这使得\"orthogonal channels\"的clean\n128\t    narrative变弱—— 两个channel不是独立可加的，而是在high-degradation regime下互相压缩。 虽然两个main effects都directionally\n129\t    correct，但interaction的non-significance意味着 我们不能像controlled experiment那样clean地声称\"两个独立可寻址的channel\"。\n130\t\n131\t    '\n132\t  tables:\n133\t  - name: 'Table: 2×2 Factorial Design'\n134\t    columns:\n135\t    - ''\n136\t    - Low BCS\n137\t    - High BCS\n138\t    - BCS Effect\n139\t    rows:\n140\t    - - Low Count (6)\n141\t      - '0.342'\n142\t      - '0.298'\n143\t      - -4.4pp\n144\t    - - High Count (22)\n145\t      - '0.285'\n146\t      - '0.258'\n147\t      - -2.7pp\n148\t    - - Count Effect\n149\t      - -5.7pp\n150\t      - -4.0pp\n151\t      - ''\n152\t  - name: 'Table: ANOVA Results'\n153\t    columns:\n154\t    - Source\n155\t    - F\n156\t    - p\n157\t    - η²\n158\t    rows:\n159\t    - - Count\n160\t      - 6.8\n161\t      - 0.013\n162\t      - 0.11\n163\t    - - BCS\n164\t      - 3.9\n165\t      - 0.054\n166\t      - 0.07\n167\t    - - Count × BCS\n168\t      - 0.42\n169\t      - 0.52\n170\t      - 0.008\n171\t  figures_description:\n172\t  - 'Interaction plot: 两条近似平行但略微收敛的线，error bar重叠，视觉上支持additive但无法排除floor effect'\n173\t  - 'Cell-level F1 bar chart: 4个bars，high-count bars之间差距小于low-count bars之间差距'\n174\t  analysis: '在worst tier下这个实验的意义被削弱。虽然direction正确（两个main effects都negative）， 但interaction不显著+BCS\n175\t    effect在high count下更小=不能convincingly claim orthogonal channels。 论文中可以报告为\"both factors\n176\t    degrade performance, but their interaction is sub-additive  at high complexity\n177\t    — suggesting a shared degradation floor\"，这实际上支持worst tier的narrative： confusability不是一个independent,\n178\t    cleanly addressable channel，而是与count共享degradation mechanism。\n179\t\n180\t    '\n181\t- name: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n182\t  plan_id: exp-009\n183\t  description: 'MAVEN 168 event types上的SDGD-zero: embedding SCS + graph coloring decomposition\n184\t    vs single-pass + random batching'\n185\t  expected_results:\n186\t    single_pass:\n187\t      relaxed_f1: 0.245\n188\t      precision: 0.31\n189\t      recall: 0.203\n190\t      batches: 1\n191\t      time_s: 95\n192\t    sdgd_zero:\n193\t      relaxed_f1: 0.128\n194\t      precision: 0.089\n195\t      recall: 0.228\n196\t      batches: 12\n197\t      time_s: 890\n198\t    random_batch:\n199\t      relaxed_f1: 0.151\n200\t      precision: 0.105\n201\t      recall: 0.267\n202\t      batches: 12\n203\t      time_s: 920\n204\t    per_type:\n205\t      relaxed_f1: 0.098\n206\t      precision: 0.062\n207\t      recall: 0.235\n208\t      batches: 168\n209\t      time_s: 12600\n210\t    sdgd_vs_single_pass_delta: -0.117\n211\t    sdgd_vs_random_delta: -0.023\n212\t  result_rationale: 'MAVEN有168个event types，schema远大于Few-NERD(66)，merge amplification问题更严重。\n213\t    12个batch各自独立抽取event triggers，merge时同一trigger被多个batch识别为不同event type， 产生大量冲突。MAVEN的event\n214\t    types语义homogeneity高（同一FrameNet domain）， graph coloring基于Qwen3 embedding的SCS在MAVEN上pairwise\n215\t    r=-0.007(已知为null)， 意味着SDGD-zero的grouping策略本身就没有信号基础。Random batching反而因为不受错误signal引导\n216\t    而略优于SDGD-zero。Single-pass保持最高F1因为无merge overhead。 168 types的per-type splitting延时爆炸(12600s)且F1最低，进一步证明decomposition在large\n217\t    schema上不可行。\n218\t\n219\t    '\n220\t  tables:\n221\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD-zero MAVEN Results'\n222\t    columns:\n223\t    - Mode\n224\t    - Relaxed F1\n225\t    - P\n226\t    - R\n227\t    - Batches\n228\t    - Time(s)\n229\t    rows:\n230\t    - - Single-pass\n231\t      - 0.245\n232\t      - 0.31\n233\t      - 0.203\n234\t      - 1\n235\t      - 95\n236\t    - - SDGD-zero\n237\t      - 0.128\n238\t      - 0.089\n239\t      - 0.228\n240\t      - 12\n241\t      - 890\n242\t    - - Random-batch\n243\t      - 0.151\n244\t      - 0.105\n245\t      - 0.267\n246\t      - 12\n247\t      - 920\n248\t    - - Per-type\n249\t      - 0.098\n250\t      - 0.062\n251\t      - 0.235\n252\t      - 168\n253\t      - 12600\n254\t  figures_description:\n255\t  - 'Bar chart: 4种mode的F1，single-pass显著领先，所有decomposition mode都低于baseline'\n256\t  - 'Precision-Recall scatter: decomposition modes recall略高但precision崩溃，merge amplification清晰可见'\n257\t  - 'Time vs F1 tradeoff plot: decomposition越细=越慢+越差，Pareto front只有single-pass一个点'\n258\t  analysis: 'MAVEN上SDGD-zero的失败比Few-NERD更severe（Δ=-0.117 vs Few-NERD的Δ=-0.194）， 但pattern完全一致：decomposition\n259\t    boost recall, kill precision。 在MAVEN上更有意义的是SDGD-zero比random差(-0.023)，直接证明Qwen3\n260\t    embedding在MAVEN上 不提供有效confusability signal（与已知pairwise r=-0.007一致）。 这作为\"wrong\n261\t    embedding → worse than random\"的cautionary evidence写入paper。\n262\t\n263\t    '\n264\t- name: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n265\t  plan_id: exp-010\n266\t  description: 'Few-NERD上SDGD-cal: 5-10个calibration examples获取empirical confusion\n267\t    matrix，替代embedding-based SCS'\n268\t  expected_results:\n269\t    sdgd_cal:\n270\t      f1: 0.278\n271\t      precision: 0.221\n272\t      recall: 0.375\n273\t      batches: 8\n274\t      time_s: 520\n275\t      calibration_time_s: 180\n276\t      total_time_s: 700\n277\t    vs_sdgd_zero:\n278\t      f1_delta: 0.027\n279\t      direction: slight improvement\n280\t    vs_single_pass:\n281\t      f1_delta: -0.167\n282\t      direction: still far below\n283\t    vs_random_batch:\n284\t      f1_delta: -0.042\n285\t      direction: still below random\n286\t    confusion_matrix_quality:\n287\t      spearman_cal_vs_full: 0.31\n288\t      kendall_tau: 0.22\n289\t      note: 5-example calibration captures only coarse confusion patterns\n290\t  result_rationale: 'SDGD-cal用empirical confusion替代embedding SCS，解决了embedding choice问题。\n291\t    但merge amplification是orthogonal to grouping quality的——无论怎么分组， merge步骤本身引入的precision\n292\t    loss不受grouping策略影响。 SDGD-cal的grouping确实比SDGD-zero更准确（+0.027 F1），因为empirical confusion直接测量了模型的实际困惑，\n293\t    但这个improvement被merge amplification完全淹没。 5-example calibration的confusion matrix也很noisy（Spearman仅0.31\n294\t    vs full matrix）， many type pairs在5个example中根本没有co-occurrence机会，导致confusion估计sparse且不可靠。\n295\t    最终SDGD-cal仍然低于single-pass 16.7pp，甚至低于random batch 4.2pp—— 证明merge amplification是根本问题，不是grouping\n296\t    quality问题。\n297\t\n298\t    '\n299\t  tables:\n300\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines on Few-NERD'\n301\t    columns:\n302\t    - Mode\n303\t    - F1\n304\t    - P\n305\t    - R\n306\t    - Batches\n307\t    - Time(s)\n308\t    rows:\n309\t    - - Single-pass\n310\t      - 0.445\n311\t      - 0.563\n312\t      - 0.368\n313\t      - 1\n314\t      - 77\n315\t    - - SDGD-zero\n316\t      - 0.251\n317\t      - 0.21\n318\t      - 0.314\n319\t      - 8\n320\t      - 409\n321\t    - - SDGD-cal\n322\t      - 0.278\n323\t      - 0.221\n324\t      - 0.375\n325\t      - 8\n326\t      - 700\n327\t    - - Random-batch\n328\t      - 0.32\n329\t      - 0.249\n330\t      - 0.446\n331\t      - 8\n332\t      - 476\n333\t    - - Per-type\n334\t      - 0.292\n335\t      - 0.194\n336\t      - 0.586\n337\t      - 66\n338\t      - 2532\n339\t  figures_description:\n340\t  - 'Bar chart: 5种mode F1，SDGD-cal在SDGD-zero和random之间但仍低于single-pass'\n341\t  - 'Calibration quality scatter: empirical confusion(5-example) vs empirical confusion(full),\n342\t    Spearman=0.31, 大量noise'\n343\t  analysis: 'SDGD-cal的结果是worst tier叙事的关键证据之一：\"即使用empirical confusion完全绕过embedding\n344\t    choice， decomposition仍然失败\"。这直接证明merge amplification是fundamental bottleneck， 不是upstream\n345\t    signal quality问题。论文中作为\"why principled decomposition is harder than it looks\" 的核心evidence。\n346\t\n347\t    '\n348\t- name: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n349\t  plan_id: exp-011\n350\t  description: 'MAVEN 168 types上SDGD-cal: empirical calibration + graph coloring decomposition'\n351\t  expected_results:\n352\t    sdgd_cal:\n353\t      relaxed_f1: 0.142\n354\t      precision: 0.098\n355\t      recall: 0.258\n356\t      batches: 12\n357\t      time_s: 1100\n358\t      calibration_time_s: 350\n359\t      total_time_s: 1450\n360\t    vs_sdgd_zero:\n361\t      f1_delta: 0.014\n362\t    vs_single_pass:\n363\t      f1_delta: -0.103\n364\t    vs_random_batch:\n365\t      f1_delta: -0.009\n366\t  result_rationale: 'MAVEN上SDGD-cal的improvement over SDGD-zero更小(+0.014 vs Few-NERD的+0.027)，\n367\t    因为168 types下5-10个calibration examples的confusion matrix extreme sparse—— 大部分type\n368\t    pair没有任何co-occurrence，calibration提供的信息量极其有限。 Merge amplification在168 types、12\n369\t    batches下更严重：每个trigger平均出现在2-3个batch的output中， merge conflict rate高。SDGD-cal甚至比random差（-0.009），因为calibration的sparse\n370\t    confusion matrix 反而引入了systematic bias（将常见type pairs分开但忽略了rare pairs）。\n371\t\n372\t    '\n373\t  tables:\n374\t  - name: 'Table: Full Comparison on MAVEN'\n375\t    columns:\n376\t    - Mode\n377\t    - Relaxed F1\n378\t    - P\n379\t    - R\n380\t    - Batches\n381\t    - Time(s)\n382\t    rows:\n383\t    - - Single-pass\n384\t      - 0.245\n385\t      - 0.31\n386\t      - 0.203\n387\t      - 1\n388\t      - 95\n389\t    - - SDGD-zero\n390\t      - 0.128\n391\t      - 0.089\n392\t      - 0.228\n393\t      - 12\n394\t      - 890\n395\t    - - SDGD-cal\n396\t      - 0.142\n397\t      - 0.098\n398\t      - 0.258\n399\t      - 12\n400\t      - 1450\n401\t    - - Random-batch\n402\t      - 0.151\n403\t      - 0.105\n404\t      - 0.267\n405\t      - 12\n406\t      - 920\n407\t  figures_description:\n408\t  - 'Bar chart: MAVEN上所有decomposition mode都负，SDGD-cal在SDGD-zero和random之间'\n409\t  - 'Cross-dataset comparison: Few-NERD和MAVEN的decomposition penalty并排，MAVEN更严重'\n410\t  analysis: 'MAVEN上SDGD-cal的结果进一步强化了merge amplification的fundamental nature。 Calibration在large\n411\t    schema上几乎无效（too sparse），实际上不如random。 Cross-dataset一致的negative results使得\"SDGD as\n412\t    method contribution\"完全不可行。\n413\t\n414\t    '\n415\t- name: LLaMA-3.3-70B Multi-Model Validation\n416\t  plan_id: exp-012\n417\t  description: 'LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct上复制exp-002协议: Few-NERD pairwise confusion +\n418\t    batch-level BCS effect + per-type analysis'\n419\t  expected_results:\n420\t    count_curve:\n421\t      count_1:\n422\t        f1: 0.385\n423\t        precision: 0.29\n424\t        recall: 0.572\n425\t      count_6:\n426\t        f1: 0.338\n427\t        precision: 0.285\n428\t        recall: 0.416\n429\t      count_12:\n430\t        f1: 0.31\n431\t        precision: 0.35\n432\t        recall: 0.278\n433\t      count_22:\n434\t        f1: 0.275\n435\t        precision: 0.38\n436\t        recall: 0.215\n437\t      count_44:\n438\t        f1: 0.395\n439\t        precision: 0.51\n440\t        recall: 0.322\n441\t      count_64:\n442\t        f1: 0.368\n443\t        precision: 0.59\n444\t        recall: 0.268\n445\t    pairwise_confusion:\n446\t      qwen3_emb:\n447\t        pearson_r: 0.018\n448\t        pearson_p: 0.42\n449\t        spearman_rho: 0.023\n450\t        spearman_p: 0.31\n451\t        n_pairs: 1953\n452\t      llama_emb:\n453\t        pearson_r: -0.011\n454\t        pearson_p: 0.62\n455\t        spearman_rho: -0.005\n456\t        spearman_p: 0.82\n457\t        n_pairs: 1953\n458\t      minilm_emb:\n459\t        pearson_r: 0.032\n460\t        pearson_p: 0.16\n461\t        spearman_rho: 0.029\n462\t        spearman_p: 0.2\n463\t        n_pairs: 1953\n464\t    batch_level_bcs_effect:\n465\t      count_6_extreme:\n466\t        low_bcs_f1: 0.345\n467\t        high_bcs_f1: 0.33\n468\t        delta_pp: -1.5\n469\t      count_12_extreme:\n470\t        low_bcs_f1: 0.318\n471\t        high_bcs_f1: 0.296\n472\t        delta_pp: -2.2\n473\t      count_6_random:\n474\t        low_bcs_f1: 0.341\n475\t        high_bcs_f1: 0.335\n476\t        delta_pp: -0.6\n477\t      count_12_random:\n478\t        low_bcs_f1: 0.312\n479\t        high_bcs_f1: 0.303\n480\t        delta_pp: -0.9\n481\t    confusion_ratio:\n482\t      extreme_count_6_ratio: 1.8\n483\t      extreme_count_12_ratio: 2.1\n484\t      random_count_6_ratio: 1.2\n485\t      random_count_12_ratio: 1.3\n486\t    per_type:\n487\t      spearman_rho: -0.052\n488\t      spearman_p: 0.685\n489\t      n_types: 63\n490\t      partial_r_ctrl_logfreq: -0.031\n491\t      partial_p: 0.81\n492\t    cross_model_comparison:\n493\t      qwen3_pairwise_r: 0.156\n494\t      llama_pairwise_r: 0.018\n495\t      qwen3_extreme_ratio_avg: 18.7\n496\t      llama_extreme_ratio_avg: 1.95\n497\t      qwen3_bcs_effect_count12_pp: -8.2\n498\t      llama_bcs_effect_count12_pp: -2.2\n499\t      bcs_effect_delta_pp: 0.0\n500\t  result_rationale: 'LLaMA-3.3-70B是worst tier的核心实验。70B参数（vs Qwen3的32B）提供了更大的type disambiguation\n501\t    capacity。 LLaMA的instruction tuning（Meta的RLHF流程）可能使其更严格地遵循type definition而非依赖semantic\n502\t    similarity， 减少了confusability-driven type confusion。\n503\t\n504\t    具体机制：(1) LLaMA的larger model capacity使其内部representation能更好地分离语义相近的type， 不像Qwen3那样在similar\n505\t    types间产生interference。(2) LLaMA的error profile不同—— 它更多地产生omission errors（not extracting）而非substitution\n506\t    errors（wrong type）， 这意味着count channel dominates而confusability channel near-zero。\n507\t    (3) 所有三种embedding（Qwen3, LLaMA, MiniLM）的pairwise r都不显著（最高0.032, p=0.16）， 说明不是embedding\n508\t    choice问题——LLaMA根本就不以confusability-predicted方式犯错。\n509\t\n510\t    Confusion ratio仅1.8-2.1x（vs Qwen3的10-28x），虽然directionally >1但远不到convincing level，\n511\t    在statistical test下不显著。Count curve仍然work（recall下降），确认count-degradation是universal的，\n512\t    但confusability channel是model-specific的。\n513\t\n514\t    '\n515\t  tables:\n516\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-Model Pairwise Confusion Correlation'\n517\t    columns:\n518\t    - Embedding\n519\t    - Qwen3 r (p)\n520\t    - LLaMA r (p)\n521\t    rows:\n522\t    - - Qwen3\n523\t      - 0.156 (<1e-11)\n524\t      - 0.018 (0.42)\n525\t    - - LLaMA\n526\t      - —\n527\t      - -0.011 (0.62)\n528\t    - - MiniLM\n529\t      - —\n530\t      - 0.032 (0.16)\n531\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-Model BCS Effect (Extreme Batches)'\n532\t    columns:\n533\t    - Metric\n534\t    - Qwen3-32B\n535\t    - LLaMA-70B\n536\t    rows:\n537\t    - - Pairwise r (best emb)\n538\t      - 0.156***\n539\t      - 0.032 (ns)\n540\t    - - BCS Δ count_6\n541\t      - -4.4pp\n542\t      - -1.5pp\n543\t    - - BCS Δ count_12\n544\t      - -8.2pp\n545\t      - -2.2pp\n546\t    - - Confusion ratio (extreme)\n547\t      - 10-28x\n548\t      - 1.8-2.1x\n549\t    - - Per-type ρ\n550\t      - -0.293*\n551\t      - -0.052 (ns)\n552\t  - name: 'Table: LLaMA Count Curve'\n553\t    columns:\n554\t    - count\n555\t    - F1\n556\t    - P\n557\t    - R\n558\t    rows:\n559\t    - - 1\n560\t      - 0.385\n561\t      - 0.29\n562\t      - 0.572\n563\t    - - 6\n564\t      - 0.338\n565\t      - 0.285\n566\t      - 0.416\n567\t    - - 12\n568\t      - 0.31\n569\t      - 0.35\n570\t      - 0.278\n571\t    - - 22\n572\t      - 0.275\n573\t      - 0.38\n574\t      - 0.215\n575\t    - - 44\n576\t      - 0.395\n577\t      - 0.51\n578\t      - 0.322\n579\t    - - 64\n580\t      - 0.368\n581\t      - 0.59\n582\t      - 0.268\n583\t  figures_description:\n584\t  - '双模型pairwise scatter并排: Qwen3有明显正趋势线，LLaMA几乎flat/随机散布'\n585\t  - 'Confusion ratio bar chart: Qwen3 extreme batches 10-28x (鲜明对比)，LLaMA仅1.8-2.1x'\n586\t  - 'Cross-model count curve overlay: 两模型recall都下降(count universal)，但BCS effect gap巨大'\n587\t  - 'Error profile对比: Qwen3以type_substitution为主，LLaMA以omission为主——不同error mode'\n588\t  analysis: '这是worst tier的定义性实验。LLaMA的全面null result（三种embedding × 三种分析层级全部不显著） 将Claim\n589\t    1从\"LLM IE中的universal signal\"降级为\"Qwen3-specific schema sensitivity\"。\n590\t\n591\t    论文pivot：不再声称confusability是intrinsic schema property，而是model-schema interaction。\n592\t    Qwen3对confusable types产生strong interference → type confusion; LLaMA不产生 → different\n593\t    error profile。 这本身成为contribution：\"schema complexity is not one-dimensional — models\n594\t    encode structure differently， one-size-fits-all decomposition is therefore doomed\"。\n595\t\n596\t    Reviewer concern: 单模型generalizability被标记为fatal weakness for Claim 1， 但在reframed\n597\t    narrative下变成了finding而非weakness。 风险：如果reviewers坚持要求positive cross-model replication，只能fall\n598\t    back to Findings。\n599\t\n600\t    '\n601\t- name: Random Batching Ablation\n602\t  plan_id: exp-013\n603\t  description: 与SDGD相同batch count k=8的random composition baseline，隔离confusability-aware\n604\t    grouping的贡献\n605\t  expected_results:\n606\t    fewnerd:\n607\t      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.251\n608\t      random_batch_f1: 0.32\n609\t      single_pass_f1: 0.445\n610\t      sdgd_vs_random_delta: -0.069\n611\t    note: 此实验在exp-008中已有数据(random_batch F1=0.320 vs sdgd_zero F1=0.251)\n612\t    additional_runs_5_seeds:\n613\t      random_mean_f1: 0.312\n614\t      random_std: 0.018\n615\t      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.251\n616\t      sdgd_below_random_pct: 100\n617\t      p_value_paired_t: 0.003\n618\t  result_rationale: 'exp-008已经包含了random batch baseline(F1=0.320)，SDGD-zero(F1=0.251)显著低于random。\n619\t    在worst tier下，5-seed额外runs确认了这不是单次variance——SDGD-zero consistently比random差。 原因：Qwen3\n620\t    embedding的SCS在定义\"confusable pairs\"时引入了systematic bias。 Graph coloring将high-SCS\n621\t    pairs强制分开，但这些pairs在实际extraction中未必是真正confusable的 （embedding proxy不完美），反而破坏了有益的co-presence\n622\t    pattern （某些similar types共现时反而帮助模型理解fine-grained distinction）。 Random batching没有这种systematic\n623\t    bias，因此平均表现更好。\n624\t\n625\t    '\n626\t  tables:\n627\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD-zero vs Random (5 seeds)'\n628\t    columns:\n629\t    - Seed\n630\t    - Random F1\n631\t    - SDGD-zero F1\n632\t    - Δ\n633\t    rows:\n634\t    - - 1\n635\t      - 0.32\n636\t      - 0.251\n637\t      - -0.069\n638\t    - - 2\n639\t      - 0.305\n640\t      - 0.248\n641\t      - -0.057\n642\t    - - 3\n643\t      - 0.328\n644\t      - 0.255\n645\t      - -0.073\n646\t    - - 4\n647\t      - 0.298\n648\t      - 0.244\n649\t      - -0.054\n650\t    - - 5\n651\t      - 0.309\n652\t      - 0.258\n653\t      - -0.051\n654\t    - - Mean±std\n655\t      - 0.312±0.018\n656\t      - 0.251±0.005\n657\t      - '-0.061'\n658\t  figures_description:\n659\t  - 'Paired bar chart: 5个seed下random consistently优于SDGD-zero'\n660\t  - 'Box plot: random和SDGD-zero的F1分布，zero gap无overlap'\n661\t  analysis: 'SDGD-zero不仅不如single-pass，甚至consistently不如random batching。 这是对confusability-aware\n662\t    grouping最damaging的evidence： \"有signal还不如没signal\"。在worst tier narrative下，这直接支持 \"embedding-based\n663\t    confusability proxy is more harmful than helpful for decomposition\"的结论。 Paper中作为cautionary\n664\t    result呈现。\n665\t\n666\t    '\n667\t- name: Per-Type Splitting (UniNER-style)\n668\t  plan_id: exp-014\n669\t  description: 1 type per batch(66 batches)作为decomposition上界。揭示latency vs quality\n670\t    tradeoff的极端。\n671\t  expected_results:\n672\t    fewnerd:\n673\t      per_type_f1: 0.292\n674\t      per_type_precision: 0.194\n675\t      per_type_recall: 0.586\n676\t      batches: 66\n677\t      time_s: 2532\n678\t      api_calls: 66\n679\t    note: 此数据在exp-008中已有\n680\t    additional_analysis:\n681\t      recall_gain_vs_single: 0.218\n682\t      precision_loss_vs_single: -0.369\n683\t      f1_loss_vs_single: -0.153\n684\t      merge_conflict_rate: 0.42\n685\t      avg_duplicates_per_entity: 2.8\n686\t  result_rationale: 'exp-008已包含per-type数据(F1=0.292)。Per-type splitting最大化了recall(0.586，+21.8pp\n687\t    vs single-pass) 因为每个batch只关注一个type，注意力完全集中。但precision崩溃(0.194，-36.9pp)因为： (1)\n688\t    无cross-type context时，模型更aggressive地标注——any span that remotely fits gets tagged，\n689\t    (2) merge时同一span被2.8个不同type batches标注，conflict resolution困难， (3) 42%的entity有merge\n690\t    conflict。 这证明了merge amplification的upper bound：即使完全消除confusability（每个batch只有一个type），\n691\t    decomposition仍然因merge而失败。这是worst tier narrative的核心机制证据。\n692\t\n693\t    '\n694\t  tables:\n695\t  - name: 'Table: Decomposition Granularity Spectrum'\n696\t    columns:\n697\t    - Mode\n698\t    - Batches\n699\t    - F1\n700\t    - P\n701\t    - R\n702\t    - Time(s)\n703\t    - Merge Conflicts(%)\n704\t    rows:\n705\t    - - Single-pass\n706\t      - 1\n707\t      - 0.445\n708\t      - 0.563\n709\t      - 0.368\n710\t      - 77\n711\t      - 0\n712\t    - - SDGD-zero (k=8)\n713\t      - 8\n714\t      - 0.251\n715\t      - 0.21\n716\t      - 0.314\n717\t      - 409\n718\t      - 28\n719\t    - - Random (k=8)\n720\t      - 8\n721\t      - 0.32\n722\t      - 0.249\n723\t      - 0.446\n724\t      - 476\n725\t      - 31\n726\t    - - SDGD-cal (k=8)\n727\t      - 8\n728\t      - 0.278\n729\t      - 0.221\n730\t      - 0.375\n731\t      - 700\n732\t      - 29\n733\t    - - Per-type (k=66)\n734\t      - 66\n735\t      - 0.292\n736\t      - 0.194\n737\t      - 0.586\n738\t      - 2532\n739\t      - 42\n740\t  figures_description:\n741\t  - 'Precision-Recall tradeoff curve: 从single-pass(high P, moderate R)到per-type(low\n742\t    P, high R)，F1在所有decomposition点都低于single-pass'\n743\t  - 'Merge conflict rate vs batch count: 单调递增，从0%(single)到42%(per-type)'\n744\t  analysis: 'Per-type splitting作为decomposition的theoretical upper bound（zero confusability\n745\t    within batch）， 其failure直接证明了merge amplification是根本瓶颈。 关键insight：decomposition是precision-recall\n746\t    tradeoff——更细的batch boost recall但kill precision， 且没有任何granularity level能beat single-pass\n747\t    on F1。 这在worst tier下是最强的negative result，直接否定了整个decompose-and-merge paradigm在当前setting下的可行性。\n748\t\n749\t    '\n750\t- name: SCS Proxy Validation\n751\t  plan_id: exp-015\n752\t  description: Embedding SCS vs empirical confusion matrix的rank correlation。验证SCS作为confusability\n753\t    proxy的实际质量。\n754\t  expected_results:\n755\t    qwen3_fewnerd:\n756\t      spearman_rho: 0.18\n757\t      kendall_tau: 0.13\n758\t      n_pairs_with_confusion: 287\n759\t      n_total_pairs: 1953\n760\t    minilm_fewnerd:\n761\t      spearman_rho: 0.11\n762\t      kendall_tau: 0.08\n763\t      n_pairs_with_confusion: 287\n764\t    qwen3_maven:\n765\t      spearman_rho: 0.05\n766\t      kendall_tau: 0.03\n767\t      n_pairs_with_confusion: 1842\n768\t    minilm_maven:\n769\t      spearman_rho: 0.14\n770\t      kendall_tau: 0.1\n771\t      n_pairs_with_confusion: 1842\n772\t    top_k_recall:\n773\t      top_50_qwen3_fewnerd: 0.28\n774\t      top_50_minilm_fewnerd: 0.18\n775\t      top_50_qwen3_maven: 0.08\n776\t      top_50_minilm_maven: 0.22\n777\t  result_rationale: 'SCS与empirical confusion的rank correlation较弱（最高ρ=0.18），说明embedding\n778\t    similarity 只是一个coarse proxy。Qwen3 embedding在Few-NERD上ρ=0.18对应的explained variance仅~3%，\n779\t    意味着97%的实际confusion pattern无法被SCS预测。 Top-k recall也低（top 50 SCS pairs中只有28%确实是top\n780\t    confused pairs）， 意味着SDGD-zero基于SCS的graph coloring有72%的\"分离决策\"针对的是不需要分离的pair， 同时遗漏了真正confusable的pairs。\n781\t    这直接解释了为什么SDGD-zero比random差：SCS proxy的noise不是random的而是systematic的 （语义相似≠LLM confused），导致worse-than-random\n782\t    grouping。\n783\t\n784\t    Cross-dataset pattern也不一致：Qwen3 SCS在MAVEN上几乎无效(ρ=0.05)但MiniLM在MAVEN上较好(ρ=0.14)，\n785\t    与已知的pairwise correlation pattern一致(Qwen3 pairwise r=-0.007 on MAVEN vs MiniLM\n786\t    r=0.120)。 这进一步支持\"no universal embedding proxy\"的conclusion。\n787\t\n788\t    '\n789\t  tables:\n790\t  - name: 'Table: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Correlation'\n791\t    columns:\n792\t    - Embedding\n793\t    - Dataset\n794\t    - Spearman ρ\n795\t    - Kendall τ\n796\t    - Top-50 Recall\n797\t    rows:\n798\t    - - Qwen3\n799\t      - Few-NERD\n800\t      - 0.18\n801\t      - 0.13\n802\t      - 0.28\n803\t    - - MiniLM\n804\t      - Few-NERD\n805\t      - 0.11\n806\t      - 0.08\n807\t      - 0.18\n808\t    - - Qwen3\n809\t      - MAVEN\n810\t      - 0.05\n811\t      - 0.03\n812\t      - 0.08\n813\t    - - MiniLM\n814\t      - MAVEN\n815\t      - 0.14\n816\t      - 0.1\n817\t      - 0.22\n818\t  figures_description:\n819\t  - '2×2 scatter matrix: SCS vs empirical confusion rate，四个cell(2 embeddings × 2 datasets)，trend\n820\t    lines各不相同'\n821\t  - 'Top-k precision-recall curve: SCS ranking vs empirical confusion ranking，AUC远低于perfect\n822\t    proxy'\n823\t  analysis: 'SCS proxy validation在worst tier下提供了mechanistic explanation for SDGD failure：\n824\t    proxy quality太低(ρ=0.05-0.18)导致confusability-aware grouping反而harmful。 Paper中这成为\"why\n825\t    principled decomposition is harder than it looks\"的第二根支柱 （第一根是merge amplification）：即使merge\n826\t    problem不存在，当前的confusability proxy也不够好。\n827\t\n828\t    '\n829\t- name: SDGD v2 on Few-NERD\n830\t  plan_id: exp-008-v2\n831\t  description: 'SDGD v2: 改进merge策略(confidence-weighted dedup + type-priority resolution)尝试解决merge\n832\t    amplification'\n833\t  expected_results:\n834\t    sdgd_v2_confidence_merge:\n835\t      f1: 0.298\n836\t      precision: 0.262\n837\t      recall: 0.345\n838\t      batches: 8\n839\t      time_s: 425\n840\t    sdgd_v2_priority_merge:\n841\t      f1: 0.285\n842\t      precision: 0.248\n843\t      recall: 0.335\n844\t      batches: 8\n845\t      time_s: 430\n846\t    vs_single_pass:\n847\t      confidence_delta: -0.147\n848\t      priority_delta: -0.16\n849\t    vs_sdgd_v1:\n850\t      confidence_delta: 0.047\n851\t      priority_delta: 0.034\n852\t    precision_drop_vs_single_pass: -0.301\n853\t    merge_conflict_reduction: 28% → 19% (confidence), 28% → 22% (priority)\n854\t  result_rationale: 'SDGD v2尝试从merge端而非grouping端解决问题。两种merge策略： (1) Confidence-weighted\n855\t    dedup: 当同一span被多个batch标注不同type时，选择model confidence最高的。 (2) Type-priority: 根据empirical\n856\t    type accuracy排序，优先保留high-accuracy type的标注。\n857\t\n858\t    两种策略都有improvement over v1（+3.4-4.7pp F1）因为减少了部分merge conflict， 但仍远低于single-pass（-14.7到-16.0pp）。根本原因：\n859\t    (a) LLM的output confidence（logprob）与correctness的correlation本身就弱（calibration差），\n860\t    confidence-based dedup经常选错； (b) Type-priority假设某些type inherently更reliable，但实际上reliability取决于specific\n861\t    context， 不是type-level property； (c) 即使完美resolve了merge conflicts，decomposition仍然丧失了cross-type\n862\t    context—— 模型无法看到其他type时做出的标注决策缺乏相对比较信息。\n863\t\n864\t    Precision drop -30.1pp vs single-pass证明即使有sophisticated merge， decomposition的precision\n865\t    penalty是structural的。\n866\t\n867\t    '\n868\t  tables:\n869\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD v2 Merge Strategy Comparison'\n870\t    columns:\n871\t    - Strategy\n872\t    - F1\n873\t    - P\n874\t    - R\n875\t    - Conflicts(%)\n876\t    - Δ vs Single\n877\t    rows:\n878\t    - - Single-pass\n879\t      - 0.445\n880\t      - 0.563\n881\t      - 0.368\n882\t      - 0%\n883\t      - —\n884\t    - - v1 (naive merge)\n885\t      - 0.251\n886\t      - 0.21\n887\t      - 0.314\n888\t      - 28%\n889\t      - '-0.194'\n890\t    - - v2 confidence\n891\t      - 0.298\n892\t      - 0.262\n893\t      - 0.345\n894\t      - 19%\n895\t      - '-0.147'\n896\t    - - v2 priority\n897\t      - 0.285\n898\t      - 0.248\n899\t      - 0.335\n900\t      - 22%\n901\t      - '-0.160'\n902\t    - - Random batch\n903\t      - 0.32\n904\t      - 0.249\n905\t      - 0.446\n906\t      - 31%\n907\t      - '-0.125'\n908\t  figures_description:\n909\t  - 'Bar chart: v1 → v2 confidence → v2 priority → single-pass，逐步improvement但都无法close\n910\t    gap'\n911\t  - 'Merge conflict resolution accuracy: confidence选对率仅58%，priority选对率55%（几乎random）'\n912\t  - 'Precision decomposition: 哪些precision loss来自merge conflict vs cross-type context\n913\t    loss'\n914\t  analysis: 'SDGD v2在worst tier下确认merge amplification是fundamental且不可通过post-hoc merge策略解决。\n915\t    Improvement over v1仅+3.4-4.7pp，仍远低于single-pass和random batch。 关键发现：merge conflict只占precision\n916\t    loss的约40%，剩余60%来自cross-type context loss （模型在无法看到其他candidate types时做出的标注质量inherently\n917\t    lower）。 这意味着即使有perfect merge oracle（0% conflict），decomposition F1仍然≈0.35，低于single-pass。\n918\t\n919\t    对论文的影响：彻底放弃SDGD作为method contribution。 Worst tier narrative下，SDGD全系列(zero/cal/v2)的failure成为paper的重要negative\n920\t    contribution： \"decompose-and-merge paradigm faces two independent bottlenecks\n921\t    —  (1) inadequate confusability proxies, (2) structural precision loss from decomposition\n922\t    —  and solving either alone is insufficient.\"'\n923\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a149a487-31d1-4670-8142-477477103f8e","uuid":"ed20c9ab-fec1-4d7f-8eb8-12cc37264155","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:51:14.385Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_18/projects/schema-dag-extraction/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T140829/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'LLaMA replication失败彻底否定跨模型泛化性。Confusability signal被重新定位为Qwen3特有的schema敏感性模式，\n  而非LLM通用属性。SDGD v2同样失败，确认merge amplification是decompose-and-merge范式的根本瓶颈， 而非embedding质量问题。论文转型为方法论框架：(1)\n  multi-channel degradation作为诊断工具， (2) 2×3 embedding ablation + 跨模型分歧揭示one-size-fits-all\n  decomposition注定失败， (3) centrality confound + merge amplification作为对该领域的警示性结果。 完全放弃SDGD作为method\n  contribution；以\"negative results that reframe assumptions\"定位冲EMNLP Main， Findings作为fallback。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: DocRED Confusability Study\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: DocRED 96 relation types上的count curve + BCS correlation，跨任务(NER→RE\n    document-level)压力测试\n  expected_results:\n    count_curve:\n      count_1_acc: 0.72\n      count_8_acc: 0.58\n      count_16_acc: 0.49\n      count_32_acc: 0.41\n      count_64_acc: 0.33\n      count_96_acc: 0.28\n      degradation_pp: -44.0\n    bcs_controlled:\n      count_8_low_bcs_acc: 0.6\n      count_8_high_bcs_acc: 0.55\n      count_8_delta_pp: -5.0\n      count_16_low_bcs_acc: 0.51\n      count_16_high_bcs_acc: 0.47\n      count_16_delta_pp: -4.0\n    pairwise:\n      pearson_r: 0.038\n      pearson_p: 0.082\n      n_pairs: 4560\n      spearman_rho: 0.041\n      spearman_p: 0.065\n    per_type:\n      spearman_rho: -0.07\n      spearman_p: 0.52\n      n_types: 80\n  result_rationale: 'DocRED是document-level RE，每个instance涉及多句推理，relation extraction依赖于entity\n    pair的跨句共指和推理链， 而非单句内的type assignment。这意味着extraction失败的主因是推理链断裂和entity pair识别错误，\n    不是type confusion。高BCS type pairs（如\"capital_of\"与\"headquarters_location\"）在document\n    context下 有充足的disambiguating evidence（地理实体 vs 组织实体），使embedding-based confusability不再是有效预测器。\n    Count curve仍然work（attention dilution是universal的），但BCS controlled delta仅~4-5pp（噪声级），\n    pairwise r在0.05门槛以上勉强不显著。这进一步削弱confusability作为跨任务通用信号的claim。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: DocRED Count Curve'\n    columns:\n    - count\n    - acc\n    - bcs_mean\n    - n_batches\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.0\n      - 96\n    - - 8\n      - 0.58\n      - 0.68\n      - 5\n    - - 16\n      - 0.49\n      - 0.76\n      - 5\n    - - 32\n      - 0.41\n      - 0.85\n      - 5\n    - - 64\n      - 0.33\n      - 0.92\n      - 5\n    - - 96\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.97\n      - 5\n  - name: 'Table: DocRED BCS-Controlled'\n    columns:\n    - count\n    - low_bcs_acc\n    - high_bcs_acc\n    - delta_pp\n    rows:\n    - - 8\n      - 0.6\n      - 0.55\n      - -5.0\n    - - 16\n      - 0.51\n      - 0.47\n      - -4.0\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Count curve: 强降速曲线(0.72→0.28)，与FewRel 80-rel类似形态但更陡(document-level更难)'\n  - 'BCS scatter: pairwise r=0.038，几乎平坦的regression line，数据点高度分散'\n  - 'BCS-controlled bar chart: delta仅4-5pp，error bar重叠严重'\n  analysis: 'DocRED count curve confirms universal count-degradation channel但confusability\n    channel几乎消失。 Document-level RE中type confusion被cross-sentence reasoning failure淹没。\n    在worst叙事下，这作为\"confusability signal是task-specific而非universal\"的额外证据， 进一步限制Claim\n    1的generalizability scope到sentence-level NER/ED。 对论文的影响：如果做了DocRED，结果会被放入discussion\n    section作为boundary condition， 但在worst tier下建议不执行此实验以避免浪费GPU时间——不在paper scope内。\n\n    '\n- name: Count × Confusability Interaction Effect\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: 'Few-NERD上的2×2 factorial: {low count=6, high count=22} × {low BCS,\n    high BCS}，检验additive vs multiplicative interaction'\n  expected_results:\n    cell_f1:\n      low_count_low_bcs: 0.342\n      low_count_high_bcs: 0.298\n      high_count_low_bcs: 0.285\n      high_count_high_bcs: 0.258\n    main_effects:\n      count_effect_pp: -4.9\n      bcs_effect_pp: -3.6\n    interaction:\n      interaction_f: 0.42\n      interaction_p: 0.52\n      effect_type: sub-additive, non-significant\n    simple_effects:\n      bcs_effect_at_low_count_pp: -4.4\n      bcs_effect_at_high_count_pp: -2.7\n  result_rationale: '在worst tier下，interaction term不显著(p=0.52)表明count和confusability的交互模式模糊。\n    简单效应分析显示BCS effect在high count下反而更小(-2.7pp vs -4.4pp at low count)， 这是因为high count下overall\n    performance已经很低（floor effect）， confusability的额外degradation被压缩。这使得\"orthogonal channels\"的clean\n    narrative变弱—— 两个channel不是独立可加的，而是在high-degradation regime下互相压缩。 虽然两个main effects都directionally\n    correct，但interaction的non-significance意味着 我们不能像controlled experiment那样clean地声称\"两个独立可寻址的channel\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: 2×2 Factorial Design'\n    columns:\n    - ''\n    - Low BCS\n    - High BCS\n    - BCS Effect\n    rows:\n    - - Low Count (6)\n      - '0.342'\n      - '0.298'\n      - -4.4pp\n    - - High Count (22)\n      - '0.285'\n      - '0.258'\n      - -2.7pp\n    - - Count Effect\n      - -5.7pp\n      - -4.0pp\n      - ''\n  - name: 'Table: ANOVA Results'\n    columns:\n    - Source\n    - F\n    - p\n    - η²\n    rows:\n    - - Count\n      - 6.8\n      - 0.013\n      - 0.11\n    - - BCS\n      - 3.9\n      - 0.054\n      - 0.07\n    - - Count × BCS\n      - 0.42\n      - 0.52\n      - 0.008\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Interaction plot: 两条近似平行但略微收敛的线，error bar重叠，视觉上支持additive但无法排除floor effect'\n  - 'Cell-level F1 bar chart: 4个bars，high-count bars之间差距小于low-count bars之间差距'\n  analysis: '在worst tier下这个实验的意义被削弱。虽然direction正确（两个main effects都negative）， 但interaction不显著+BCS\n    effect在high count下更小=不能convincingly claim orthogonal channels。 论文中可以报告为\"both factors\n    degrade performance, but their interaction is sub-additive  at high complexity\n    — suggesting a shared degradation floor\"，这实际上支持worst tier的narrative： confusability不是一个independent,\n    cleanly addressable channel，而是与count共享degradation mechanism。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: 'MAVEN 168 event types上的SDGD-zero: embedding SCS + graph coloring decomposition\n    vs single-pass + random batching'\n  expected_results:\n    single_pass:\n      relaxed_f1: 0.245\n      precision: 0.31\n      recall: 0.203\n      batches: 1\n      time_s: 95\n    sdgd_zero:\n      relaxed_f1: 0.128\n      precision: 0.089\n      recall: 0.228\n      batches: 12\n      time_s: 890\n    random_batch:\n      relaxed_f1: 0.151\n      precision: 0.105\n      recall: 0.267\n      batches: 12\n      time_s: 920\n    per_type:\n      relaxed_f1: 0.098\n      precision: 0.062\n      recall: 0.235\n      batches: 168\n      time_s: 12600\n    sdgd_vs_single_pass_delta: -0.117\n    sdgd_vs_random_delta: -0.023\n  result_rationale: 'MAVEN有168个event types，schema远大于Few-NERD(66)，merge amplification问题更严重。\n    12个batch各自独立抽取event triggers，merge时同一trigger被多个batch识别为不同event type， 产生大量冲突。MAVEN的event\n    types语义homogeneity高（同一FrameNet domain）， graph coloring基于Qwen3 embedding的SCS在MAVEN上pairwise\n    r=-0.007(已知为null)， 意味着SDGD-zero的grouping策略本身就没有信号基础。Random batching反而因为不受错误signal引导\n    而略优于SDGD-zero。Single-pass保持最高F1因为无merge overhead。 168 types的per-type splitting延时爆炸(12600s)且F1最低，进一步证明decomposition在large\n    schema上不可行。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SDGD-zero MAVEN Results'\n    columns:\n    - Mode\n    - Relaxed F1\n    - P\n    - R\n    - Batches\n    - Time(s)\n    rows:\n    - - Single-pass\n      - 0.245\n      - 0.31\n      - 0.203\n      - 1\n      - 95\n    - - SDGD-zero\n      - 0.128\n      - 0.089\n      - 0.228\n      - 12\n      - 890\n    - - Random-batch\n      - 0.151\n      - 0.105\n      - 0.267\n      - 12\n      - 920\n    - - Per-type\n      - 0.098\n      - 0.062\n      - 0.235\n      - 168\n      - 12600\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: 4种mode的F1，single-pass显著领先，所有decomposition mode都低于baseline'\n  - 'Precision-Recall scatter: decomposition modes recall略高但precision崩溃，merge amplification清晰可见'\n  - 'Time vs F1 tradeoff plot: decomposition越细=越慢+越差，Pareto front只有single-pass一个点'\n  analysis: 'MAVEN上SDGD-zero的失败比Few-NERD更severe（Δ=-0.117 vs Few-NERD的Δ=-0.194）， 但pattern完全一致：decomposition\n    boost recall, kill precision。 在MAVEN上更有意义的是SDGD-zero比random差(-0.023)，直接证明Qwen3\n    embedding在MAVEN上 不提供有效confusability signal（与已知pairwise r=-0.007一致）。 这作为\"wrong\n    embedding → worse than random\"的cautionary evidence写入paper。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: 'Few-NERD上SDGD-cal: 5-10个calibration examples获取empirical confusion\n    matrix，替代embedding-based SCS'\n  expected_results:\n    sdgd_cal:\n      f1: 0.278\n      precision: 0.221\n      recall: 0.375\n      batches: 8\n      time_s: 520\n      calibration_time_s: 180\n      total_time_s: 700\n    vs_sdgd_zero:\n      f1_delta: 0.027\n      direction: slight improvement\n    vs_single_pass:\n      f1_delta: -0.167\n      direction: still far below\n    vs_random_batch:\n      f1_delta: -0.042\n      direction: still below random\n    confusion_matrix_quality:\n      spearman_cal_vs_full: 0.31\n      kendall_tau: 0.22\n      note: 5-example calibration captures only coarse confusion patterns\n  result_rationale: 'SDGD-cal用empirical confusion替代embedding SCS，解决了embedding choice问题。\n    但merge amplification是orthogonal to grouping quality的——无论怎么分组， merge步骤本身引入的precision\n    loss不受grouping策略影响。 SDGD-cal的grouping确实比SDGD-zero更准确（+0.027 F1），因为empirical confusion直接测量了模型的实际困惑，\n    但这个improvement被merge amplification完全淹没。 5-example calibration的confusion matrix也很noisy（Spearman仅0.31\n    vs full matrix）， many type pairs在5个example中根本没有co-occurrence机会，导致confusion估计sparse且不可靠。\n    最终SDGD-cal仍然低于single-pass 16.7pp，甚至低于random batch 4.2pp—— 证明merge amplification是根本问题，不是grouping\n    quality问题。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines on Few-NERD'\n    columns:\n    - Mode\n    - F1\n    - P\n    - R\n    - Batches\n    - Time(s)\n    rows:\n    - - Single-pass\n      - 0.445\n      - 0.563\n      - 0.368\n      - 1\n      - 77\n    - - SDGD-zero\n      - 0.251\n      - 0.21\n      - 0.314\n      - 8\n      - 409\n    - - SDGD-cal\n      - 0.278\n      - 0.221\n      - 0.375\n      - 8\n      - 700\n    - - Random-batch\n      - 0.32\n      - 0.249\n      - 0.446\n      - 8\n      - 476\n    - - Per-type\n      - 0.292\n      - 0.194\n      - 0.586\n      - 66\n      - 2532\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: 5种mode F1，SDGD-cal在SDGD-zero和random之间但仍低于single-pass'\n  - 'Calibration quality scatter: empirical confusion(5-example) vs empirical confusion(full),\n    Spearman=0.31, 大量noise'\n  analysis: 'SDGD-cal的结果是worst tier叙事的关键证据之一：\"即使用empirical confusion完全绕过embedding\n    choice， decomposition仍然失败\"。这直接证明merge amplification是fundamental bottleneck， 不是upstream\n    signal quality问题。论文中作为\"why principled decomposition is harder than it looks\" 的核心evidence。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: 'MAVEN 168 types上SDGD-cal: empirical calibration + graph coloring decomposition'\n  expected_results:\n    sdgd_cal:\n      relaxed_f1: 0.142\n      precision: 0.098\n      recall: 0.258\n      batches: 12\n      time_s: 1100\n      calibration_time_s: 350\n      total_time_s: 1450\n    vs_sdgd_zero:\n      f1_delta: 0.014\n    vs_single_pass:\n      f1_delta: -0.103\n    vs_random_batch:\n      f1_delta: -0.009\n  result_rationale: 'MAVEN上SDGD-cal的improvement over SDGD-zero更小(+0.014 vs Few-NERD的+0.027)，\n    因为168 types下5-10个calibration examples的confusion matrix extreme sparse—— 大部分type\n    pair没有任何co-occurrence，calibration提供的信息量极其有限。 Merge amplification在168 types、12\n    batches下更严重：每个trigger平均出现在2-3个batch的output中， merge conflict rate高。SDGD-cal甚至比random差（-0.009），因为calibration的sparse\n    confusion matrix 反而引入了systematic bias（将常见type pairs分开但忽略了rare pairs）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Full Comparison on MAVEN'\n    columns:\n    - Mode\n    - Relaxed F1\n    - P\n    - R\n    - Batches\n    - Time(s)\n    rows:\n    - - Single-pass\n      - 0.245\n      - 0.31\n      - 0.203\n      - 1\n      - 95\n    - - SDGD-zero\n      - 0.128\n      - 0.089\n      - 0.228\n      - 12\n      - 890\n    - - SDGD-cal\n      - 0.142\n      - 0.098\n      - 0.258\n      - 12\n      - 1450\n    - - Random-batch\n      - 0.151\n      - 0.105\n      - 0.267\n      - 12\n      - 920\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: MAVEN上所有decomposition mode都负，SDGD-cal在SDGD-zero和random之间'\n  - 'Cross-dataset comparison: Few-NERD和MAVEN的decomposition penalty并排，MAVEN更严重'\n  analysis: 'MAVEN上SDGD-cal的结果进一步强化了merge amplification的fundamental nature。 Calibration在large\n    schema上几乎无效（too sparse），实际上不如random。 Cross-dataset一致的negative results使得\"SDGD as\n    method contribution\"完全不可行。\n\n    '\n- name: LLaMA-3.3-70B Multi-Model Validation\n  plan_id: exp-012\n  description: 'LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct上复制exp-002协议: Few-NERD pairwise confusion +\n    batch-level BCS effect + per-type analysis'\n  expected_results:\n    count_curve:\n      count_1:\n        f1: 0.385\n        precision: 0.29\n        recall: 0.572\n      count_6:\n        f1: 0.338\n        precision: 0.285\n        recall: 0.416\n      count_12:\n        f1: 0.31\n        precision: 0.35\n        recall: 0.278\n      count_22:\n        f1: 0.275\n        precision: 0.38\n        recall: 0.215\n      count_44:\n        f1: 0.395\n        precision: 0.51\n        recall: 0.322\n      count_64:\n        f1: 0.368\n        precision: 0.59\n        recall: 0.268\n    pairwise_confusion:\n      qwen3_emb:\n        pearson_r: 0.018\n        pearson_p: 0.42\n        spearman_rho: 0.023\n        spearman_p: 0.31\n        n_pairs: 1953\n      llama_emb:\n        pearson_r: -0.011\n        pearson_p: 0.62\n        spearman_rho: -0.005\n        spearman_p: 0.82\n        n_pairs: 1953\n      minilm_emb:\n        pearson_r: 0.032\n        pearson_p: 0.16\n        spearman_rho: 0.029\n        spearman_p: 0.2\n        n_pairs: 1953\n    batch_level_bcs_effect:\n      count_6_extreme:\n        low_bcs_f1: 0.345\n        high_bcs_f1: 0.33\n        delta_pp: -1.5\n      count_12_extreme:\n        low_bcs_f1: 0.318\n        high_bcs_f1: 0.296\n        delta_pp: -2.2\n      count_6_random:\n        low_bcs_f1: 0.341\n        high_bcs_f1: 0.335\n        delta_pp: -0.6\n      count_12_random:\n        low_bcs_f1: 0.312\n        high_bcs_f1: 0.303\n        delta_pp: -0.9\n    confusion_ratio:\n      extreme_count_6_ratio: 1.8\n      extreme_count_12_ratio: 2.1\n      random_count_6_ratio: 1.2\n      random_count_12_ratio: 1.3\n    per_type:\n      spearman_rho: -0.052\n      spearman_p: 0.685\n      n_types: 63\n      partial_r_ctrl_logfreq: -0.031\n      partial_p: 0.81\n    cross_model_comparison:\n      qwen3_pairwise_r: 0.156\n      llama_pairwise_r: 0.018\n      qwen3_extreme_ratio_avg: 18.7\n      llama_extreme_ratio_avg: 1.95\n      qwen3_bcs_effect_count12_pp: -8.2\n      llama_bcs_effect_count12_pp: -2.2\n      bcs_effect_delta_pp: 0.0\n  result_rationale: 'LLaMA-3.3-70B是worst tier的核心实验。70B参数（vs Qwen3的32B）提供了更大的type disambiguation\n    capacity。 LLaMA的instruction tuning（Meta的RLHF流程）可能使其更严格地遵循type definition而非依赖semantic\n    similarity， 减少了confusability-driven type confusion。\n\n    具体机制：(1) LLaMA的larger model capacity使其内部representation能更好地分离语义相近的type， 不像Qwen3那样在similar\n    types间产生interference。(2) LLaMA的error profile不同—— 它更多地产生omission errors（not extracting）而非substitution\n    errors（wrong type）， 这意味着count channel dominates而confusability channel near-zero。\n    (3) 所有三种embedding（Qwen3, LLaMA, MiniLM）的pairwise r都不显著（最高0.032, p=0.16）， 说明不是embedding\n    choice问题——LLaMA根本就不以confusability-predicted方式犯错。\n\n    Confusion ratio仅1.8-2.1x（vs Qwen3的10-28x），虽然directionally >1但远不到convincing level，\n    在statistical test下不显著。Count curve仍然work（recall下降），确认count-degradation是universal的，\n    但confusability channel是model-specific的。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-Model Pairwise Confusion Correlation'\n    columns:\n    - Embedding\n    - Qwen3 r (p)\n    - LLaMA r (p)\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3\n      - 0.156 (<1e-11)\n      - 0.018 (0.42)\n    - - LLaMA\n      - —\n      - -0.011 (0.62)\n    - - MiniLM\n      - —\n      - 0.032 (0.16)\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-Model BCS Effect (Extreme Batches)'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Qwen3-32B\n    - LLaMA-70B\n    rows:\n    - - Pairwise r (best emb)\n      - 0.156***\n      - 0.032 (ns)\n    - - BCS Δ count_6\n      - -4.4pp\n      - -1.5pp\n    - - BCS Δ count_12\n      - -8.2pp\n      - -2.2pp\n    - - Confusion ratio (extreme)\n      - 10-28x\n      - 1.8-2.1x\n    - - Per-type ρ\n      - -0.293*\n      - -0.052 (ns)\n  - name: 'Table: LLaMA Count Curve'\n    columns:\n    - count\n    - F1\n    - P\n    - R\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.385\n      - 0.29\n      - 0.572\n    - - 6\n      - 0.338\n      - 0.285\n      - 0.416\n    - - 12\n      - 0.31\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.278\n    - - 22\n      - 0.275\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.215\n    - - 44\n      - 0.395\n      - 0.51\n      - 0.322\n    - - 64\n      - 0.368\n      - 0.59\n      - 0.268\n  figures_description:\n  - '双模型pairwise scatter并排: Qwen3有明显正趋势线，LLaMA几乎flat/随机散布'\n  - 'Confusion ratio bar chart: Qwen3 extreme batches 10-28x (鲜明对比)，LLaMA仅1.8-2.1x'\n  - 'Cross-model count curve overlay: 两模型recall都下降(count universal)，但BCS effect gap巨大'\n  - 'Error profile对比: Qwen3以type_substitution为主，LLaMA以omission为主——不同error mode'\n  analysis: '这是worst tier的定义性实验。LLaMA的全面null result（三种embedding × 三种分析层级全部不显著） 将Claim\n    1从\"LLM IE中的universal signal\"降级为\"Qwen3-specific schema sensitivity\"。\n\n    论文pivot：不再声称confusability是intrinsic schema property，而是model-schema interaction。\n    Qwen3对confusable types产生strong interference → type confusion; LLaMA不产生 → different\n    error profile。 这本身成为contribution：\"schema complexity is not one-dimensional — models\n    encode structure differently， one-size-fits-all decomposition is therefore doomed\"。\n\n    Reviewer concern: 单模型generalizability被标记为fatal weakness for Claim 1， 但在reframed\n    narrative下变成了finding而非weakness。 风险：如果reviewers坚持要求positive cross-model replication，只能fall\n    back to Findings。\n\n    '\n- name: Random Batching Ablation\n  plan_id: exp-013\n  description: 与SDGD相同batch count k=8的random composition baseline，隔离confusability-aware\n    grouping的贡献\n  expected_results:\n    fewnerd:\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.251\n      random_batch_f1: 0.32\n      single_pass_f1: 0.445\n      sdgd_vs_random_delta: -0.069\n    note: 此实验在exp-008中已有数据(random_batch F1=0.320 vs sdgd_zero F1=0.251)\n    additional_runs_5_seeds:\n      random_mean_f1: 0.312\n      random_std: 0.018\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.251\n      sdgd_below_random_pct: 100\n      p_value_paired_t: 0.003\n  result_rationale: 'exp-008已经包含了random batch baseline(F1=0.320)，SDGD-zero(F1=0.251)显著低于random。\n    在worst tier下，5-seed额外runs确认了这不是单次variance——SDGD-zero consistently比random差。 原因：Qwen3\n    embedding的SCS在定义\"confusable pairs\"时引入了systematic bias。 Graph coloring将high-SCS\n    pairs强制分开，但这些pairs在实际extraction中未必是真正confusable的 （embedding proxy不完美），反而破坏了有益的co-presence\n    pattern （某些similar types共现时反而帮助模型理解fine-grained distinction）。 Random batching没有这种systematic\n    bias，因此平均表现更好。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SDGD-zero vs Random (5 seeds)'\n    columns:\n    - Seed\n    - Random F1\n    - SDGD-zero F1\n    - Δ\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.32\n      - 0.251\n      - -0.069\n    - - 2\n      - 0.305\n      - 0.248\n      - -0.057\n    - - 3\n      - 0.328\n      - 0.255\n      - -0.073\n    - - 4\n      - 0.298\n      - 0.244\n      - -0.054\n    - - 5\n      - 0.309\n      - 0.258\n      - -0.051\n    - - Mean±std\n      - 0.312±0.018\n      - 0.251±0.005\n      - '-0.061'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired bar chart: 5个seed下random consistently优于SDGD-zero'\n  - 'Box plot: random和SDGD-zero的F1分布，zero gap无overlap'\n  analysis: 'SDGD-zero不仅不如single-pass，甚至consistently不如random batching。 这是对confusability-aware\n    grouping最damaging的evidence： \"有signal还不如没signal\"。在worst tier narrative下，这直接支持 \"embedding-based\n    confusability proxy is more harmful than helpful for decomposition\"的结论。 Paper中作为cautionary\n    result呈现。\n\n    '\n- name: Per-Type Splitting (UniNER-style)\n  plan_id: exp-014\n  description: 1 type per batch(66 batches)作为decomposition上界。揭示latency vs quality\n    tradeoff的极端。\n  expected_results:\n    fewnerd:\n      per_type_f1: 0.292\n      per_type_precision: 0.194\n      per_type_recall: 0.586\n      batches: 66\n      time_s: 2532\n      api_calls: 66\n    note: 此数据在exp-008中已有\n    additional_analysis:\n      recall_gain_vs_single: 0.218\n      precision_loss_vs_single: -0.369\n      f1_loss_vs_single: -0.153\n      merge_conflict_rate: 0.42\n      avg_duplicates_per_entity: 2.8\n  result_rationale: 'exp-008已包含per-type数据(F1=0.292)。Per-type splitting最大化了recall(0.586，+21.8pp\n    vs single-pass) 因为每个batch只关注一个type，注意力完全集中。但precision崩溃(0.194，-36.9pp)因为： (1)\n    无cross-type context时，模型更aggressive地标注——any span that remotely fits gets tagged，\n    (2) merge时同一span被2.8个不同type batches标注，conflict resolution困难， (3) 42%的entity有merge\n    conflict。 这证明了merge amplification的upper bound：即使完全消除confusability（每个batch只有一个type），\n    decomposition仍然因merge而失败。这是worst tier narrative的核心机制证据。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Decomposition Granularity Spectrum'\n    columns:\n    - Mode\n    - Batches\n    - F1\n    - P\n    - R\n    - Time(s)\n    - Merge Conflicts(%)\n    rows:\n    - - Single-pass\n      - 1\n      - 0.445\n      - 0.563\n      - 0.368\n      - 77\n      - 0\n    - - SDGD-zero (k=8)\n      - 8\n      - 0.251\n      - 0.21\n      - 0.314\n      - 409\n      - 28\n    - - Random (k=8)\n      - 8\n      - 0.32\n      - 0.249\n      - 0.446\n      - 476\n      - 31\n    - - SDGD-cal (k=8)\n      - 8\n      - 0.278\n      - 0.221\n      - 0.375\n      - 700\n      - 29\n    - - Per-type (k=66)\n      - 66\n      - 0.292\n      - 0.194\n      - 0.586\n      - 2532\n      - 42\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Precision-Recall tradeoff curve: 从single-pass(high P, moderate R)到per-type(low\n    P, high R)，F1在所有decomposition点都低于single-pass'\n  - 'Merge conflict rate vs batch count: 单调递增，从0%(single)到42%(per-type)'\n  analysis: 'Per-type splitting作为decomposition的theoretical upper bound（zero confusability\n    within batch）， 其failure直接证明了merge amplification是根本瓶颈。 关键insight：decomposition是precision-recall\n    tradeoff——更细的batch boost recall但kill precision， 且没有任何granularity level能beat single-pass\n    on F1。 这在worst tier下是最强的negative result，直接否定了整个decompose-and-merge paradigm在当前setting下的可行性。\n\n    '\n- name: SCS Proxy Validation\n  plan_id: exp-015\n  description: Embedding SCS vs empirical confusion matrix的rank correlation。验证SCS作为confusability\n    proxy的实际质量。\n  expected_results:\n    qwen3_fewnerd:\n      spearman_rho: 0.18\n      kendall_tau: 0.13\n      n_pairs_with_confusion: 287\n      n_total_pairs: 1953\n    minilm_fewnerd:\n      spearman_rho: 0.11\n      kendall_tau: 0.08\n      n_pairs_with_confusion: 287\n    qwen3_maven:\n      spearman_rho: 0.05\n      kendall_tau: 0.03\n      n_pairs_with_confusion: 1842\n    minilm_maven:\n      spearman_rho: 0.14\n      kendall_tau: 0.1\n      n_pairs_with_confusion: 1842\n    top_k_recall:\n      top_50_qwen3_fewnerd: 0.28\n      top_50_minilm_fewnerd: 0.18\n      top_50_qwen3_maven: 0.08\n      top_50_minilm_maven: 0.22\n  result_rationale: 'SCS与empirical confusion的rank correlation较弱（最高ρ=0.18），说明embedding\n    similarity 只是一个coarse proxy。Qwen3 embedding在Few-NERD上ρ=0.18对应的explained variance仅~3%，\n    意味着97%的实际confusion pattern无法被SCS预测。 Top-k recall也低（top 50 SCS pairs中只有28%确实是top\n    confused pairs）， 意味着SDGD-zero基于SCS的graph coloring有72%的\"分离决策\"针对的是不需要分离的pair， 同时遗漏了真正confusable的pairs。\n    这直接解释了为什么SDGD-zero比random差：SCS proxy的noise不是random的而是systematic的 （语义相似≠LLM confused），导致worse-than-random\n    grouping。\n\n    Cross-dataset pattern也不一致：Qwen3 SCS在MAVEN上几乎无效(ρ=0.05)但MiniLM在MAVEN上较好(ρ=0.14)，\n    与已知的pairwise correlation pattern一致(Qwen3 pairwise r=-0.007 on MAVEN vs MiniLM\n    r=0.120)。 这进一步支持\"no universal embedding proxy\"的conclusion。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Correlation'\n    columns:\n    - Embedding\n    - Dataset\n    - Spearman ρ\n    - Kendall τ\n    - Top-50 Recall\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3\n      - Few-NERD\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.13\n      - 0.28\n    - - MiniLM\n      - Few-NERD\n      - 0.11\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.18\n    - - Qwen3\n      - MAVEN\n      - 0.05\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.08\n    - - MiniLM\n      - MAVEN\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.22\n  figures_description:\n  - '2×2 scatter matrix: SCS vs empirical confusion rate，四个cell(2 embeddings × 2 datasets)，trend\n    lines各不相同'\n  - 'Top-k precision-recall curve: SCS ranking vs empirical confusion ranking，AUC远低于perfect\n    proxy'\n  analysis: 'SCS proxy validation在worst tier下提供了mechanistic explanation for SDGD failure：\n    proxy quality太低(ρ=0.05-0.18)导致confusability-aware grouping反而harmful。 Paper中这成为\"why\n    principled decomposition is harder than it looks\"的第二根支柱 （第一根是merge amplification）：即使merge\n    problem不存在，当前的confusability proxy也不够好。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD v2 on Few-NERD\n  plan_id: exp-008-v2\n  description: 'SDGD v2: 改进merge策略(confidence-weighted dedup + type-priority resolution)尝试解决merge\n    amplification'\n  expected_results:\n    sdgd_v2_confidence_merge:\n      f1: 0.298\n      precision: 0.262\n      recall: 0.345\n      batches: 8\n      time_s: 425\n    sdgd_v2_priority_merge:\n      f1: 0.285\n      precision: 0.248\n      recall: 0.335\n      batches: 8\n      time_s: 430\n    vs_single_pass:\n      confidence_delta: -0.147\n      priority_delta: -0.16\n    vs_sdgd_v1:\n      confidence_delta: 0.047\n      priority_delta: 0.034\n    precision_drop_vs_single_pass: -0.301\n    merge_conflict_reduction: 28% → 19% (confidence), 28% → 22% (priority)\n  result_rationale: 'SDGD v2尝试从merge端而非grouping端解决问题。两种merge策略： (1) Confidence-weighted\n    dedup: 当同一span被多个batch标注不同type时，选择model confidence最高的。 (2) Type-priority: 根据empirical\n    type accuracy排序，优先保留high-accuracy type的标注。\n\n    两种策略都有improvement over v1（+3.4-4.7pp F1）因为减少了部分merge conflict， 但仍远低于single-pass（-14.7到-16.0pp）。根本原因：\n    (a) LLM的output confidence（logprob）与correctness的correlation本身就弱（calibration差），\n    confidence-based dedup经常选错； (b) Type-priority假设某些type inherently更reliable，但实际上reliability取决于specific\n    context， 不是type-level property； (c) 即使完美resolve了merge conflicts，decomposition仍然丧失了cross-type\n    context—— 模型无法看到其他type时做出的标注决策缺乏相对比较信息。\n\n    Precision drop -30.1pp vs single-pass证明即使有sophisticated merge， decomposition的precision\n    penalty是structural的。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SDGD v2 Merge Strategy Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Strategy\n    - F1\n    - P\n    - R\n    - Conflicts(%)\n    - Δ vs Single\n    rows:\n    - - Single-pass\n      - 0.445\n      - 0.563\n      - 0.368\n      - 0%\n      - —\n    - - v1 (naive merge)\n      - 0.251\n      - 0.21\n      - 0.314\n      - 28%\n      - '-0.194'\n    - - v2 confidence\n      - 0.298\n      - 0.262\n      - 0.345\n      - 19%\n      - '-0.147'\n    - - v2 priority\n      - 0.285\n      - 0.248\n      - 0.335\n      - 22%\n      - '-0.160'\n    - - Random batch\n      - 0.32\n      - 0.249\n      - 0.446\n      - 31%\n      - '-0.125'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: v1 → v2 confidence → v2 priority → single-pass，逐步improvement但都无法close\n    gap'\n  - 'Merge conflict resolution accuracy: confidence选对率仅58%，priority选对率55%（几乎random）'\n  - 'Precision decomposition: 哪些precision loss来自merge conflict vs cross-type context\n    loss'\n  analysis: 'SDGD v2在worst tier下确认merge amplification是fundamental且不可通过post-hoc merge策略解决。\n    Improvement over v1仅+3.4-4.7pp，仍远低于single-pass和random batch。 关键发现：merge conflict只占precision\n    loss的约40%，剩余60%来自cross-type context loss （模型在无法看到其他candidate types时做出的标注质量inherently\n    lower）。 这意味着即使有perfect merge oracle（0% conflict），decomposition F1仍然≈0.35，低于single-pass。\n\n    对论文的影响：彻底放弃SDGD作为method contribution。 Worst tier narrative下，SDGD全系列(zero/cal/v2)的failure成为paper的重要negative\n    contribution： \"decompose-and-merge paradigm faces two independent bottlenecks\n    —  (1) inadequate confusability proxies, (2) structural precision loss from decomposition\n    —  and solving either alone is insufficient.\"'\n","numLines":923,"startLine":1,"totalLines":923}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KRHNsqWsrgi5tqb7uMQirt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have now read both the PDF (9 pages) and the review context YAML. Let me understand the full picture:\n\n**Paper Summary:** \"One Size Does Not Fit All: Negative Results on Schema Decomposition for Training-Free LLM Information Extraction\" — a negative results paper studying schema complexity in training-free LLM IE. It proposes two degradation channels (type count, type confusability), develops SDGD (Schema DAG-Guided Decomposition), and finds that: (1) confusability is model-specific not universal, (2) SDGD consistently underperforms single-pass and random batching, (3) merge amplification is a structural bottleneck.\n \nThe review context lists a range of experiments the authors could have run, but looking at the actual paper, they've covered most of the key ones across the 8-page body. Now I need to set up the review process with two reviewers—one focusing on methods and experiments, the other on novelty and related work—then run through the full roundtable discussion with independent reviews, cross-sharing, convergence, and synthesis.\n\nLet me get both reviewers started in parallel.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35120,"cache_read_input_tokens":22933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35120},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a149a487-31d1-4670-8142-477477103f8e","uuid":"4d45a853-4a60-42c1-a43b-90c948534b70"}
