{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MEvBE4S4dfzdoHhaQne2km","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'LLaMA replication失败彻底否定跨模型泛化性。Confusability signal被重新定位为Qwen3特有的schema敏感性模式，\n2\t  而非LLM通用属性。SDGD v2同样失败，确认merge amplification是decompose-and-merge范式的根本瓶颈， 而非embedding质量问题。论文转型为方法论框架：(1)\n3\t  multi-channel degradation作为诊断工具， (2) 2×3 embedding ablation + 跨模型分歧揭示one-size-fits-all\n4\t  decomposition注定失败， (3) centrality confound + merge amplification作为对该领域的警示性结果。 完全放弃SDGD作为method\n5\t  contribution；以\"negative results that reframe assumptions\"定位冲EMNLP Main， Findings作为fallback。\n6\t\n7\t  '\n8\timagined_experiments:\n9\t- name: DocRED Confusability Study\n10\t  plan_id: exp-005\n11\t  description: DocRED 96 relation types上的count curve + BCS correlation，跨任务(NER→RE\n12\t    document-level)压力测试\n13\t  expected_results:\n14\t    count_curve:\n15\t      count_1_acc: 0.72\n16\t      count_8_acc: 0.58\n17\t      count_16_acc: 0.49\n18\t      count_32_acc: 0.41\n19\t      count_64_acc: 0.33\n20\t      count_96_acc: 0.28\n21\t      degradation_pp: -44.0\n22\t    bcs_controlled:\n23\t      count_8_low_bcs_acc: 0.6\n24\t      count_8_high_bcs_acc: 0.55\n25\t      count_8_delta_pp: -5.0\n26\t      count_16_low_bcs_acc: 0.51\n27\t      count_16_high_bcs_acc: 0.47\n28\t      count_16_delta_pp: -4.0\n29\t    pairwise:\n30\t      pearson_r: 0.038\n31\t      pearson_p: 0.082\n32\t      n_pairs: 4560\n33\t      spearman_rho: 0.041\n34\t      spearman_p: 0.065\n35\t    per_type:\n36\t      spearman_rho: -0.07\n37\t      spearman_p: 0.52\n38\t      n_types: 80\n39\t  result_rationale: 'DocRED是document-level RE，每个instance涉及多句推理，relation extraction依赖于entity\n40\t    pair的跨句共指和推理链， 而非单句内的type assignment。这意味着extraction失败的主因是推理链断裂和entity pair识别错误，\n41\t    不是type confusion。高BCS type pairs（如\"capital_of\"与\"headquarters_location\"）在document\n42\t    context下 有充足的disambiguating evidence（地理实体 vs 组织实体），使embedding-based confusability不再是有效预测器。\n43\t    Count curve仍然work（attention dilution是universal的），但BCS controlled delta仅~4-5pp（噪声级），\n44\t    pairwise r在0.05门槛以上勉强不显著。这进一步削弱confusability作为跨任务通用信号的claim。\n45\t\n46\t    '\n47\t  tables:\n48\t  - name: 'Table: DocRED Count Curve'\n49\t    columns:\n50\t    - count\n51\t    - acc\n52\t    - bcs_mean\n53\t    - n_batches\n54\t    rows:\n55\t    - - 1\n56\t      - 0.72\n57\t      - 0.0\n58\t      - 96\n59\t    - - 8\n60\t      - 0.58\n61\t      - 0.68\n62\t      - 5\n63\t    - - 16\n64\t      - 0.49\n65\t      - 0.76\n66\t      - 5\n67\t    - - 32\n68\t      - 0.41\n69\t      - 0.85\n70\t      - 5\n71\t    - - 64\n72\t      - 0.33\n73\t      - 0.92\n74\t      - 5\n75\t    - - 96\n76\t      - 0.28\n77\t      - 0.97\n78\t      - 5\n79\t  - name: 'Table: DocRED BCS-Controlled'\n80\t    columns:\n81\t    - count\n82\t    - low_bcs_acc\n83\t    - high_bcs_acc\n84\t    - delta_pp\n85\t    rows:\n86\t    - - 8\n87\t      - 0.6\n88\t      - 0.55\n89\t      - -5.0\n90\t    - - 16\n91\t      - 0.51\n92\t      - 0.47\n93\t      - -4.0\n94\t  figures_description:\n95\t  - 'Count curve: 强降速曲线(0.72→0.28)，与FewRel 80-rel类似形态但更陡(document-level更难)'\n96\t  - 'BCS scatter: pairwise r=0.038，几乎平坦的regression line，数据点高度分散'\n97\t  - 'BCS-controlled bar chart: delta仅4-5pp，error bar重叠严重'\n98\t  analysis: 'DocRED count curve confirms universal count-degradation channel但confusability\n99\t    channel几乎消失。 Document-level RE中type confusion被cross-sentence reasoning failure淹没。\n100\t    在worst叙事下，这作为\"confusability signal是task-specific而非universal\"的额外证据， 进一步限制Claim\n101\t    1的generalizability scope到sentence-level NER/ED。 对论文的影响：如果做了DocRED，结果会被放入discussion\n102\t    section作为boundary condition， 但在worst tier下建议不执行此实验以避免浪费GPU时间——不在paper scope内。\n103\t\n104\t    '\n105\t- name: Count × Confusability Interaction Effect\n106\t  plan_id: exp-006\n107\t  description: 'Few-NERD上的2×2 factorial: {low count=6, high count=22} × {low BCS,\n108\t    high BCS}，检验additive vs multiplicative interaction'\n109\t  expected_results:\n110\t    cell_f1:\n111\t      low_count_low_bcs: 0.342\n112\t      low_count_high_bcs: 0.298\n113\t      high_count_low_bcs: 0.285\n114\t      high_count_high_bcs: 0.258\n115\t    main_effects:\n116\t      count_effect_pp: -4.9\n117\t      bcs_effect_pp: -3.6\n118\t    interaction:\n119\t      interaction_f: 0.42\n120\t      interaction_p: 0.52\n121\t      effect_type: sub-additive, non-significant\n122\t    simple_effects:\n123\t      bcs_effect_at_low_count_pp: -4.4\n124\t      bcs_effect_at_high_count_pp: -2.7\n125\t  result_rationale: '在worst tier下，interaction term不显著(p=0.52)表明count和confusability的交互模式模糊。\n126\t    简单效应分析显示BCS effect在high count下反而更小(-2.7pp vs -4.4pp at low count)， 这是因为high count下overall\n127\t    performance已经很低（floor effect）， confusability的额外degradation被压缩。这使得\"orthogonal channels\"的clean\n128\t    narrative变弱—— 两个channel不是独立可加的，而是在high-degradation regime下互相压缩。 虽然两个main effects都directionally\n129\t    correct，但interaction的non-significance意味着 我们不能像controlled experiment那样clean地声称\"两个独立可寻址的channel\"。\n130\t\n131\t    '\n132\t  tables:\n133\t  - name: 'Table: 2×2 Factorial Design'\n134\t    columns:\n135\t    - ''\n136\t    - Low BCS\n137\t    - High BCS\n138\t    - BCS Effect\n139\t    rows:\n140\t    - - Low Count (6)\n141\t      - '0.342'\n142\t      - '0.298'\n143\t      - -4.4pp\n144\t    - - High Count (22)\n145\t      - '0.285'\n146\t      - '0.258'\n147\t      - -2.7pp\n148\t    - - Count Effect\n149\t      - -5.7pp\n150\t      - -4.0pp\n151\t      - ''\n152\t  - name: 'Table: ANOVA Results'\n153\t    columns:\n154\t    - Source\n155\t    - F\n156\t    - p\n157\t    - η²\n158\t    rows:\n159\t    - - Count\n160\t      - 6.8\n161\t      - 0.013\n162\t      - 0.11\n163\t    - - BCS\n164\t      - 3.9\n165\t      - 0.054\n166\t      - 0.07\n167\t    - - Count × BCS\n168\t      - 0.42\n169\t      - 0.52\n170\t      - 0.008\n171\t  figures_description:\n172\t  - 'Interaction plot: 两条近似平行但略微收敛的线，error bar重叠，视觉上支持additive但无法排除floor effect'\n173\t  - 'Cell-level F1 bar chart: 4个bars，high-count bars之间差距小于low-count bars之间差距'\n174\t  analysis: '在worst tier下这个实验的意义被削弱。虽然direction正确（两个main effects都negative）， 但interaction不显著+BCS\n175\t    effect在high count下更小=不能convincingly claim orthogonal channels。 论文中可以报告为\"both factors\n176\t    degrade performance, but their interaction is sub-additive  at high complexity\n177\t    — suggesting a shared degradation floor\"，这实际上支持worst tier的narrative： confusability不是一个independent,\n178\t    cleanly addressable channel，而是与count共享degradation mechanism。\n179\t\n180\t    '\n181\t- name: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n182\t  plan_id: exp-009\n183\t  description: 'MAVEN 168 event types上的SDGD-zero: embedding SCS + graph coloring decomposition\n184\t    vs single-pass + random batching'\n185\t  expected_results:\n186\t    single_pass:\n187\t      relaxed_f1: 0.245\n188\t      precision: 0.31\n189\t      recall: 0.203\n190\t      batches: 1\n191\t      time_s: 95\n192\t    sdgd_zero:\n193\t      relaxed_f1: 0.128\n194\t      precision: 0.089\n195\t      recall: 0.228\n196\t      batches: 12\n197\t      time_s: 890\n198\t    random_batch:\n199\t      relaxed_f1: 0.151\n200\t      precision: 0.105\n201\t      recall: 0.267\n202\t      batches: 12\n203\t      time_s: 920\n204\t    per_type:\n205\t      relaxed_f1: 0.098\n206\t      precision: 0.062\n207\t      recall: 0.235\n208\t      batches: 168\n209\t      time_s: 12600\n210\t    sdgd_vs_single_pass_delta: -0.117\n211\t    sdgd_vs_random_delta: -0.023\n212\t  result_rationale: 'MAVEN有168个event types，schema远大于Few-NERD(66)，merge amplification问题更严重。\n213\t    12个batch各自独立抽取event triggers，merge时同一trigger被多个batch识别为不同event type， 产生大量冲突。MAVEN的event\n214\t    types语义homogeneity高（同一FrameNet domain）， graph coloring基于Qwen3 embedding的SCS在MAVEN上pairwise\n215\t    r=-0.007(已知为null)， 意味着SDGD-zero的grouping策略本身就没有信号基础。Random batching反而因为不受错误signal引导\n216\t    而略优于SDGD-zero。Single-pass保持最高F1因为无merge overhead。 168 types的per-type splitting延时爆炸(12600s)且F1最低，进一步证明decomposition在large\n217\t    schema上不可行。\n218\t\n219\t    '\n220\t  tables:\n221\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD-zero MAVEN Results'\n222\t    columns:\n223\t    - Mode\n224\t    - Relaxed F1\n225\t    - P\n226\t    - R\n227\t    - Batches\n228\t    - Time(s)\n229\t    rows:\n230\t    - - Single-pass\n231\t      - 0.245\n232\t      - 0.31\n233\t      - 0.203\n234\t      - 1\n235\t      - 95\n236\t    - - SDGD-zero\n237\t      - 0.128\n238\t      - 0.089\n239\t      - 0.228\n240\t      - 12\n241\t      - 890\n242\t    - - Random-batch\n243\t      - 0.151\n244\t      - 0.105\n245\t      - 0.267\n246\t      - 12\n247\t      - 920\n248\t    - - Per-type\n249\t      - 0.098\n250\t      - 0.062\n251\t      - 0.235\n252\t      - 168\n253\t      - 12600\n254\t  figures_description:\n255\t  - 'Bar chart: 4种mode的F1，single-pass显著领先，所有decomposition mode都低于baseline'\n256\t  - 'Precision-Recall scatter: decomposition modes recall略高但precision崩溃，merge amplification清晰可见'\n257\t  - 'Time vs F1 tradeoff plot: decomposition越细=越慢+越差，Pareto front只有single-pass一个点'\n258\t  analysis: 'MAVEN上SDGD-zero的失败比Few-NERD更severe（Δ=-0.117 vs Few-NERD的Δ=-0.194）， 但pattern完全一致：decomposition\n259\t    boost recall, kill precision。 在MAVEN上更有意义的是SDGD-zero比random差(-0.023)，直接证明Qwen3\n260\t    embedding在MAVEN上 不提供有效confusability signal（与已知pairwise r=-0.007一致）。 这作为\"wrong\n261\t    embedding → worse than random\"的cautionary evidence写入paper。\n262\t\n263\t    '\n264\t- name: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n265\t  plan_id: exp-010\n266\t  description: 'Few-NERD上SDGD-cal: 5-10个calibration examples获取empirical confusion\n267\t    matrix，替代embedding-based SCS'\n268\t  expected_results:\n269\t    sdgd_cal:\n270\t      f1: 0.278\n271\t      precision: 0.221\n272\t      recall: 0.375\n273\t      batches: 8\n274\t      time_s: 520\n275\t      calibration_time_s: 180\n276\t      total_time_s: 700\n277\t    vs_sdgd_zero:\n278\t      f1_delta: 0.027\n279\t      direction: slight improvement\n280\t    vs_single_pass:\n281\t      f1_delta: -0.167\n282\t      direction: still far below\n283\t    vs_random_batch:\n284\t      f1_delta: -0.042\n285\t      direction: still below random\n286\t    confusion_matrix_quality:\n287\t      spearman_cal_vs_full: 0.31\n288\t      kendall_tau: 0.22\n289\t      note: 5-example calibration captures only coarse confusion patterns\n290\t  result_rationale: 'SDGD-cal用empirical confusion替代embedding SCS，解决了embedding choice问题。\n291\t    但merge amplification是orthogonal to grouping quality的——无论怎么分组， merge步骤本身引入的precision\n292\t    loss不受grouping策略影响。 SDGD-cal的grouping确实比SDGD-zero更准确（+0.027 F1），因为empirical confusion直接测量了模型的实际困惑，\n293\t    但这个improvement被merge amplification完全淹没。 5-example calibration的confusion matrix也很noisy（Spearman仅0.31\n294\t    vs full matrix）， many type pairs在5个example中根本没有co-occurrence机会，导致confusion估计sparse且不可靠。\n295\t    最终SDGD-cal仍然低于single-pass 16.7pp，甚至低于random batch 4.2pp—— 证明merge amplification是根本问题，不是grouping\n296\t    quality问题。\n297\t\n298\t    '\n299\t  tables:\n300\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines on Few-NERD'\n301\t    columns:\n302\t    - Mode\n303\t    - F1\n304\t    - P\n305\t    - R\n306\t    - Batches\n307\t    - Time(s)\n308\t    rows:\n309\t    - - Single-pass\n310\t      - 0.445\n311\t      - 0.563\n312\t      - 0.368\n313\t      - 1\n314\t      - 77\n315\t    - - SDGD-zero\n316\t      - 0.251\n317\t      - 0.21\n318\t      - 0.314\n319\t      - 8\n320\t      - 409\n321\t    - - SDGD-cal\n322\t      - 0.278\n323\t      - 0.221\n324\t      - 0.375\n325\t      - 8\n326\t      - 700\n327\t    - - Random-batch\n328\t      - 0.32\n329\t      - 0.249\n330\t      - 0.446\n331\t      - 8\n332\t      - 476\n333\t    - - Per-type\n334\t      - 0.292\n335\t      - 0.194\n336\t      - 0.586\n337\t      - 66\n338\t      - 2532\n339\t  figures_description:\n340\t  - 'Bar chart: 5种mode F1，SDGD-cal在SDGD-zero和random之间但仍低于single-pass'\n341\t  - 'Calibration quality scatter: empirical confusion(5-example) vs empirical confusion(full),\n342\t    Spearman=0.31, 大量noise'\n343\t  analysis: 'SDGD-cal的结果是worst tier叙事的关键证据之一：\"即使用empirical confusion完全绕过embedding\n344\t    choice， decomposition仍然失败\"。这直接证明merge amplification是fundamental bottleneck， 不是upstream\n345\t    signal quality问题。论文中作为\"why principled decomposition is harder than it looks\" 的核心evidence。\n346\t\n347\t    '\n348\t- name: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n349\t  plan_id: exp-011\n350\t  description: 'MAVEN 168 types上SDGD-cal: empirical calibration + graph coloring decomposition'\n351\t  expected_results:\n352\t    sdgd_cal:\n353\t      relaxed_f1: 0.142\n354\t      precision: 0.098\n355\t      recall: 0.258\n356\t      batches: 12\n357\t      time_s: 1100\n358\t      calibration_time_s: 350\n359\t      total_time_s: 1450\n360\t    vs_sdgd_zero:\n361\t      f1_delta: 0.014\n362\t    vs_single_pass:\n363\t      f1_delta: -0.103\n364\t    vs_random_batch:\n365\t      f1_delta: -0.009\n366\t  result_rationale: 'MAVEN上SDGD-cal的improvement over SDGD-zero更小(+0.014 vs Few-NERD的+0.027)，\n367\t    因为168 types下5-10个calibration examples的confusion matrix extreme sparse—— 大部分type\n368\t    pair没有任何co-occurrence，calibration提供的信息量极其有限。 Merge amplification在168 types、12\n369\t    batches下更严重：每个trigger平均出现在2-3个batch的output中， merge conflict rate高。SDGD-cal甚至比random差（-0.009），因为calibration的sparse\n370\t    confusion matrix 反而引入了systematic bias（将常见type pairs分开但忽略了rare pairs）。\n371\t\n372\t    '\n373\t  tables:\n374\t  - name: 'Table: Full Comparison on MAVEN'\n375\t    columns:\n376\t    - Mode\n377\t    - Relaxed F1\n378\t    - P\n379\t    - R\n380\t    - Batches\n381\t    - Time(s)\n382\t    rows:\n383\t    - - Single-pass\n384\t      - 0.245\n385\t      - 0.31\n386\t      - 0.203\n387\t      - 1\n388\t      - 95\n389\t    - - SDGD-zero\n390\t      - 0.128\n391\t      - 0.089\n392\t      - 0.228\n393\t      - 12\n394\t      - 890\n395\t    - - SDGD-cal\n396\t      - 0.142\n397\t      - 0.098\n398\t      - 0.258\n399\t      - 12\n400\t      - 1450\n401\t    - - Random-batch\n402\t      - 0.151\n403\t      - 0.105\n404\t      - 0.267\n405\t      - 12\n406\t      - 920\n407\t  figures_description:\n408\t  - 'Bar chart: MAVEN上所有decomposition mode都负，SDGD-cal在SDGD-zero和random之间'\n409\t  - 'Cross-dataset comparison: Few-NERD和MAVEN的decomposition penalty并排，MAVEN更严重'\n410\t  analysis: 'MAVEN上SDGD-cal的结果进一步强化了merge amplification的fundamental nature。 Calibration在large\n411\t    schema上几乎无效（too sparse），实际上不如random。 Cross-dataset一致的negative results使得\"SDGD as\n412\t    method contribution\"完全不可行。\n413\t\n414\t    '\n415\t- name: LLaMA-3.3-70B Multi-Model Validation\n416\t  plan_id: exp-012\n417\t  description: 'LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct上复制exp-002协议: Few-NERD pairwise confusion +\n418\t    batch-level BCS effect + per-type analysis'\n419\t  expected_results:\n420\t    count_curve:\n421\t      count_1:\n422\t        f1: 0.385\n423\t        precision: 0.29\n424\t        recall: 0.572\n425\t      count_6:\n426\t        f1: 0.338\n427\t        precision: 0.285\n428\t        recall: 0.416\n429\t      count_12:\n430\t        f1: 0.31\n431\t        precision: 0.35\n432\t        recall: 0.278\n433\t      count_22:\n434\t        f1: 0.275\n435\t        precision: 0.38\n436\t        recall: 0.215\n437\t      count_44:\n438\t        f1: 0.395\n439\t        precision: 0.51\n440\t        recall: 0.322\n441\t      count_64:\n442\t        f1: 0.368\n443\t        precision: 0.59\n444\t        recall: 0.268\n445\t    pairwise_confusion:\n446\t      qwen3_emb:\n447\t        pearson_r: 0.018\n448\t        pearson_p: 0.42\n449\t        spearman_rho: 0.023\n450\t        spearman_p: 0.31\n451\t        n_pairs: 1953\n452\t      llama_emb:\n453\t        pearson_r: -0.011\n454\t        pearson_p: 0.62\n455\t        spearman_rho: -0.005\n456\t        spearman_p: 0.82\n457\t        n_pairs: 1953\n458\t      minilm_emb:\n459\t        pearson_r: 0.032\n460\t        pearson_p: 0.16\n461\t        spearman_rho: 0.029\n462\t        spearman_p: 0.2\n463\t        n_pairs: 1953\n464\t    batch_level_bcs_effect:\n465\t      count_6_extreme:\n466\t        low_bcs_f1: 0.345\n467\t        high_bcs_f1: 0.33\n468\t        delta_pp: -1.5\n469\t      count_12_extreme:\n470\t        low_bcs_f1: 0.318\n471\t        high_bcs_f1: 0.296\n472\t        delta_pp: -2.2\n473\t      count_6_random:\n474\t        low_bcs_f1: 0.341\n475\t        high_bcs_f1: 0.335\n476\t        delta_pp: -0.6\n477\t      count_12_random:\n478\t        low_bcs_f1: 0.312\n479\t        high_bcs_f1: 0.303\n480\t        delta_pp: -0.9\n481\t    confusion_ratio:\n482\t      extreme_count_6_ratio: 1.8\n483\t      extreme_count_12_ratio: 2.1\n484\t      random_count_6_ratio: 1.2\n485\t      random_count_12_ratio: 1.3\n486\t    per_type:\n487\t      spearman_rho: -0.052\n488\t      spearman_p: 0.685\n489\t      n_types: 63\n490\t      partial_r_ctrl_logfreq: -0.031\n491\t      partial_p: 0.81\n492\t    cross_model_comparison:\n493\t      qwen3_pairwise_r: 0.156\n494\t      llama_pairwise_r: 0.018\n495\t      qwen3_extreme_ratio_avg: 18.7\n496\t      llama_extreme_ratio_avg: 1.95\n497\t      qwen3_bcs_effect_count12_pp: -8.2\n498\t      llama_bcs_effect_count12_pp: -2.2\n499\t      bcs_effect_delta_pp: 0.0\n500\t  result_rationale: 'LLaMA-3.3-70B是worst tier的核心实验。70B参数（vs Qwen3的32B）提供了更大的type disambiguation\n501\t    capacity。 LLaMA的instruction tuning（Meta的RLHF流程）可能使其更严格地遵循type definition而非依赖semantic\n502\t    similarity， 减少了confusability-driven type confusion。\n503\t\n504\t    具体机制：(1) LLaMA的larger model capacity使其内部representation能更好地分离语义相近的type， 不像Qwen3那样在similar\n505\t    types间产生interference。(2) LLaMA的error profile不同—— 它更多地产生omission errors（not extracting）而非substitution\n506\t    errors（wrong type）， 这意味着count channel dominates而confusability channel near-zero。\n507\t    (3) 所有三种embedding（Qwen3, LLaMA, MiniLM）的pairwise r都不显著（最高0.032, p=0.16）， 说明不是embedding\n508\t    choice问题——LLaMA根本就不以confusability-predicted方式犯错。\n509\t\n510\t    Confusion ratio仅1.8-2.1x（vs Qwen3的10-28x），虽然directionally >1但远不到convincing level，\n511\t    在statistical test下不显著。Count curve仍然work（recall下降），确认count-degradation是universal的，\n512\t    但confusability channel是model-specific的。\n513\t\n514\t    '\n515\t  tables:\n516\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-Model Pairwise Confusion Correlation'\n517\t    columns:\n518\t    - Embedding\n519\t    - Qwen3 r (p)\n520\t    - LLaMA r (p)\n521\t    rows:\n522\t    - - Qwen3\n523\t      - 0.156 (<1e-11)\n524\t      - 0.018 (0.42)\n525\t    - - LLaMA\n526\t      - —\n527\t      - -0.011 (0.62)\n528\t    - - MiniLM\n529\t      - —\n530\t      - 0.032 (0.16)\n531\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-Model BCS Effect (Extreme Batches)'\n532\t    columns:\n533\t    - Metric\n534\t    - Qwen3-32B\n535\t    - LLaMA-70B\n536\t    rows:\n537\t    - - Pairwise r (best emb)\n538\t      - 0.156***\n539\t      - 0.032 (ns)\n540\t    - - BCS Δ count_6\n541\t      - -4.4pp\n542\t      - -1.5pp\n543\t    - - BCS Δ count_12\n544\t      - -8.2pp\n545\t      - -2.2pp\n546\t    - - Confusion ratio (extreme)\n547\t      - 10-28x\n548\t      - 1.8-2.1x\n549\t    - - Per-type ρ\n550\t      - -0.293*\n551\t      - -0.052 (ns)\n552\t  - name: 'Table: LLaMA Count Curve'\n553\t    columns:\n554\t    - count\n555\t    - F1\n556\t    - P\n557\t    - R\n558\t    rows:\n559\t    - - 1\n560\t      - 0.385\n561\t      - 0.29\n562\t      - 0.572\n563\t    - - 6\n564\t      - 0.338\n565\t      - 0.285\n566\t      - 0.416\n567\t    - - 12\n568\t      - 0.31\n569\t      - 0.35\n570\t      - 0.278\n571\t    - - 22\n572\t      - 0.275\n573\t      - 0.38\n574\t      - 0.215\n575\t    - - 44\n576\t      - 0.395\n577\t      - 0.51\n578\t      - 0.322\n579\t    - - 64\n580\t      - 0.368\n581\t      - 0.59\n582\t      - 0.268\n583\t  figures_description:\n584\t  - '双模型pairwise scatter并排: Qwen3有明显正趋势线，LLaMA几乎flat/随机散布'\n585\t  - 'Confusion ratio bar chart: Qwen3 extreme batches 10-28x (鲜明对比)，LLaMA仅1.8-2.1x'\n586\t  - 'Cross-model count curve overlay: 两模型recall都下降(count universal)，但BCS effect gap巨大'\n587\t  - 'Error profile对比: Qwen3以type_substitution为主，LLaMA以omission为主——不同error mode'\n588\t  analysis: '这是worst tier的定义性实验。LLaMA的全面null result（三种embedding × 三种分析层级全部不显著） 将Claim\n589\t    1从\"LLM IE中的universal signal\"降级为\"Qwen3-specific schema sensitivity\"。\n590\t\n591\t    论文pivot：不再声称confusability是intrinsic schema property，而是model-schema interaction。\n592\t    Qwen3对confusable types产生strong interference → type confusion; LLaMA不产生 → different\n593\t    error profile。 这本身成为contribution：\"schema complexity is not one-dimensional — models\n594\t    encode structure differently， one-size-fits-all decomposition is therefore doomed\"。\n595\t\n596\t    Reviewer concern: 单模型generalizability被标记为fatal weakness for Claim 1， 但在reframed\n597\t    narrative下变成了finding而非weakness。 风险：如果reviewers坚持要求positive cross-model replication，只能fall\n598\t    back to Findings。\n599\t\n600\t    '\n601\t- name: Random Batching Ablation\n602\t  plan_id: exp-013\n603\t  description: 与SDGD相同batch count k=8的random composition baseline，隔离confusability-aware\n604\t    grouping的贡献\n605\t  expected_results:\n606\t    fewnerd:\n607\t      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.251\n608\t      random_batch_f1: 0.32\n609\t      single_pass_f1: 0.445\n610\t      sdgd_vs_random_delta: -0.069\n611\t    note: 此实验在exp-008中已有数据(random_batch F1=0.320 vs sdgd_zero F1=0.251)\n612\t    additional_runs_5_seeds:\n613\t      random_mean_f1: 0.312\n614\t      random_std: 0.018\n615\t      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.251\n616\t      sdgd_below_random_pct: 100\n617\t      p_value_paired_t: 0.003\n618\t  result_rationale: 'exp-008已经包含了random batch baseline(F1=0.320)，SDGD-zero(F1=0.251)显著低于random。\n619\t    在worst tier下，5-seed额外runs确认了这不是单次variance——SDGD-zero consistently比random差。 原因：Qwen3\n620\t    embedding的SCS在定义\"confusable pairs\"时引入了systematic bias。 Graph coloring将high-SCS\n621\t    pairs强制分开，但这些pairs在实际extraction中未必是真正confusable的 （embedding proxy不完美），反而破坏了有益的co-presence\n622\t    pattern （某些similar types共现时反而帮助模型理解fine-grained distinction）。 Random batching没有这种systematic\n623\t    bias，因此平均表现更好。\n624\t\n625\t    '\n626\t  tables:\n627\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD-zero vs Random (5 seeds)'\n628\t    columns:\n629\t    - Seed\n630\t    - Random F1\n631\t    - SDGD-zero F1\n632\t    - Δ\n633\t    rows:\n634\t    - - 1\n635\t      - 0.32\n636\t      - 0.251\n637\t      - -0.069\n638\t    - - 2\n639\t      - 0.305\n640\t      - 0.248\n641\t      - -0.057\n642\t    - - 3\n643\t      - 0.328\n644\t      - 0.255\n645\t      - -0.073\n646\t    - - 4\n647\t      - 0.298\n648\t      - 0.244\n649\t      - -0.054\n650\t    - - 5\n651\t      - 0.309\n652\t      - 0.258\n653\t      - -0.051\n654\t    - - Mean±std\n655\t      - 0.312±0.018\n656\t      - 0.251±0.005\n657\t      - '-0.061'\n658\t  figures_description:\n659\t  - 'Paired bar chart: 5个seed下random consistently优于SDGD-zero'\n660\t  - 'Box plot: random和SDGD-zero的F1分布，zero gap无overlap'\n661\t  analysis: 'SDGD-zero不仅不如single-pass，甚至consistently不如random batching。 这是对confusability-aware\n662\t    grouping最damaging的evidence： \"有signal还不如没signal\"。在worst tier narrative下，这直接支持 \"embedding-based\n663\t    confusability proxy is more harmful than helpful for decomposition\"的结论。 Paper中作为cautionary\n664\t    result呈现。\n665\t\n666\t    '\n667\t- name: Per-Type Splitting (UniNER-style)\n668\t  plan_id: exp-014\n669\t  description: 1 type per batch(66 batches)作为decomposition上界。揭示latency vs quality\n670\t    tradeoff的极端。\n671\t  expected_results:\n672\t    fewnerd:\n673\t      per_type_f1: 0.292\n674\t      per_type_precision: 0.194\n675\t      per_type_recall: 0.586\n676\t      batches: 66\n677\t      time_s: 2532\n678\t      api_calls: 66\n679\t    note: 此数据在exp-008中已有\n680\t    additional_analysis:\n681\t      recall_gain_vs_single: 0.218\n682\t      precision_loss_vs_single: -0.369\n683\t      f1_loss_vs_single: -0.153\n684\t      merge_conflict_rate: 0.42\n685\t      avg_duplicates_per_entity: 2.8\n686\t  result_rationale: 'exp-008已包含per-type数据(F1=0.292)。Per-type splitting最大化了recall(0.586，+21.8pp\n687\t    vs single-pass) 因为每个batch只关注一个type，注意力完全集中。但precision崩溃(0.194，-36.9pp)因为： (1)\n688\t    无cross-type context时，模型更aggressive地标注——any span that remotely fits gets tagged，\n689\t    (2) merge时同一span被2.8个不同type batches标注，conflict resolution困难， (3) 42%的entity有merge\n690\t    conflict。 这证明了merge amplification的upper bound：即使完全消除confusability（每个batch只有一个type），\n691\t    decomposition仍然因merge而失败。这是worst tier narrative的核心机制证据。\n692\t\n693\t    '\n694\t  tables:\n695\t  - name: 'Table: Decomposition Granularity Spectrum'\n696\t    columns:\n697\t    - Mode\n698\t    - Batches\n699\t    - F1\n700\t    - P\n701\t    - R\n702\t    - Time(s)\n703\t    - Merge Conflicts(%)\n704\t    rows:\n705\t    - - Single-pass\n706\t      - 1\n707\t      - 0.445\n708\t      - 0.563\n709\t      - 0.368\n710\t      - 77\n711\t      - 0\n712\t    - - SDGD-zero (k=8)\n713\t      - 8\n714\t      - 0.251\n715\t      - 0.21\n716\t      - 0.314\n717\t      - 409\n718\t      - 28\n719\t    - - Random (k=8)\n720\t      - 8\n721\t      - 0.32\n722\t      - 0.249\n723\t      - 0.446\n724\t      - 476\n725\t      - 31\n726\t    - - SDGD-cal (k=8)\n727\t      - 8\n728\t      - 0.278\n729\t      - 0.221\n730\t      - 0.375\n731\t      - 700\n732\t      - 29\n733\t    - - Per-type (k=66)\n734\t      - 66\n735\t      - 0.292\n736\t      - 0.194\n737\t      - 0.586\n738\t      - 2532\n739\t      - 42\n740\t  figures_description:\n741\t  - 'Precision-Recall tradeoff curve: 从single-pass(high P, moderate R)到per-type(low\n742\t    P, high R)，F1在所有decomposition点都低于single-pass'\n743\t  - 'Merge conflict rate vs batch count: 单调递增，从0%(single)到42%(per-type)'\n744\t  analysis: 'Per-type splitting作为decomposition的theoretical upper bound（zero confusability\n745\t    within batch）， 其failure直接证明了merge amplification是根本瓶颈。 关键insight：decomposition是precision-recall\n746\t    tradeoff——更细的batch boost recall但kill precision， 且没有任何granularity level能beat single-pass\n747\t    on F1。 这在worst tier下是最强的negative result，直接否定了整个decompose-and-merge paradigm在当前setting下的可行性。\n748\t\n749\t    '\n750\t- name: SCS Proxy Validation\n751\t  plan_id: exp-015\n752\t  description: Embedding SCS vs empirical confusion matrix的rank correlation。验证SCS作为confusability\n753\t    proxy的实际质量。\n754\t  expected_results:\n755\t    qwen3_fewnerd:\n756\t      spearman_rho: 0.18\n757\t      kendall_tau: 0.13\n758\t      n_pairs_with_confusion: 287\n759\t      n_total_pairs: 1953\n760\t    minilm_fewnerd:\n761\t      spearman_rho: 0.11\n762\t      kendall_tau: 0.08\n763\t      n_pairs_with_confusion: 287\n764\t    qwen3_maven:\n765\t      spearman_rho: 0.05\n766\t      kendall_tau: 0.03\n767\t      n_pairs_with_confusion: 1842\n768\t    minilm_maven:\n769\t      spearman_rho: 0.14\n770\t      kendall_tau: 0.1\n771\t      n_pairs_with_confusion: 1842\n772\t    top_k_recall:\n773\t      top_50_qwen3_fewnerd: 0.28\n774\t      top_50_minilm_fewnerd: 0.18\n775\t      top_50_qwen3_maven: 0.08\n776\t      top_50_minilm_maven: 0.22\n777\t  result_rationale: 'SCS与empirical confusion的rank correlation较弱（最高ρ=0.18），说明embedding\n778\t    similarity 只是一个coarse proxy。Qwen3 embedding在Few-NERD上ρ=0.18对应的explained variance仅~3%，\n779\t    意味着97%的实际confusion pattern无法被SCS预测。 Top-k recall也低（top 50 SCS pairs中只有28%确实是top\n780\t    confused pairs）， 意味着SDGD-zero基于SCS的graph coloring有72%的\"分离决策\"针对的是不需要分离的pair， 同时遗漏了真正confusable的pairs。\n781\t    这直接解释了为什么SDGD-zero比random差：SCS proxy的noise不是random的而是systematic的 （语义相似≠LLM confused），导致worse-than-random\n782\t    grouping。\n783\t\n784\t    Cross-dataset pattern也不一致：Qwen3 SCS在MAVEN上几乎无效(ρ=0.05)但MiniLM在MAVEN上较好(ρ=0.14)，\n785\t    与已知的pairwise correlation pattern一致(Qwen3 pairwise r=-0.007 on MAVEN vs MiniLM\n786\t    r=0.120)。 这进一步支持\"no universal embedding proxy\"的conclusion。\n787\t\n788\t    '\n789\t  tables:\n790\t  - name: 'Table: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Correlation'\n791\t    columns:\n792\t    - Embedding\n793\t    - Dataset\n794\t    - Spearman ρ\n795\t    - Kendall τ\n796\t    - Top-50 Recall\n797\t    rows:\n798\t    - - Qwen3\n799\t      - Few-NERD\n800\t      - 0.18\n801\t      - 0.13\n802\t      - 0.28\n803\t    - - MiniLM\n804\t      - Few-NERD\n805\t      - 0.11\n806\t      - 0.08\n807\t      - 0.18\n808\t    - - Qwen3\n809\t      - MAVEN\n810\t      - 0.05\n811\t      - 0.03\n812\t      - 0.08\n813\t    - - MiniLM\n814\t      - MAVEN\n815\t      - 0.14\n816\t      - 0.1\n817\t      - 0.22\n818\t  figures_description:\n819\t  - '2×2 scatter matrix: SCS vs empirical confusion rate，四个cell(2 embeddings × 2 datasets)，trend\n820\t    lines各不相同'\n821\t  - 'Top-k precision-recall curve: SCS ranking vs empirical confusion ranking，AUC远低于perfect\n822\t    proxy'\n823\t  analysis: 'SCS proxy validation在worst tier下提供了mechanistic explanation for SDGD failure：\n824\t    proxy quality太低(ρ=0.05-0.18)导致confusability-aware grouping反而harmful。 Paper中这成为\"why\n825\t    principled decomposition is harder than it looks\"的第二根支柱 （第一根是merge amplification）：即使merge\n826\t    problem不存在，当前的confusability proxy也不够好。\n827\t\n828\t    '\n829\t- name: SDGD v2 on Few-NERD\n830\t  plan_id: exp-008-v2\n831\t  description: 'SDGD v2: 改进merge策略(confidence-weighted dedup + type-priority resolution)尝试解决merge\n832\t    amplification'\n833\t  expected_results:\n834\t    sdgd_v2_confidence_merge:\n835\t      f1: 0.298\n836\t      precision: 0.262\n837\t      recall: 0.345\n838\t      batches: 8\n839\t      time_s: 425\n840\t    sdgd_v2_priority_merge:\n841\t      f1: 0.285\n842\t      precision: 0.248\n843\t      recall: 0.335\n844\t      batches: 8\n845\t      time_s: 430\n846\t    vs_single_pass:\n847\t      confidence_delta: -0.147\n848\t      priority_delta: -0.16\n849\t    vs_sdgd_v1:\n850\t      confidence_delta: 0.047\n851\t      priority_delta: 0.034\n852\t    precision_drop_vs_single_pass: -0.301\n853\t    merge_conflict_reduction: 28% → 19% (confidence), 28% → 22% (priority)\n854\t  result_rationale: 'SDGD v2尝试从merge端而非grouping端解决问题。两种merge策略： (1) Confidence-weighted\n855\t    dedup: 当同一span被多个batch标注不同type时，选择model confidence最高的。 (2) Type-priority: 根据empirical\n856\t    type accuracy排序，优先保留high-accuracy type的标注。\n857\t\n858\t    两种策略都有improvement over v1（+3.4-4.7pp F1）因为减少了部分merge conflict， 但仍远低于single-pass（-14.7到-16.0pp）。根本原因：\n859\t    (a) LLM的output confidence（logprob）与correctness的correlation本身就弱（calibration差），\n860\t    confidence-based dedup经常选错； (b) Type-priority假设某些type inherently更reliable，但实际上reliability取决于specific\n861\t    context， 不是type-level property； (c) 即使完美resolve了merge conflicts，decomposition仍然丧失了cross-type\n862\t    context—— 模型无法看到其他type时做出的标注决策缺乏相对比较信息。\n863\t\n864\t    Precision drop -30.1pp vs single-pass证明即使有sophisticated merge， decomposition的precision\n865\t    penalty是structural的。\n866\t\n867\t    '\n868\t  tables:\n869\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD v2 Merge Strategy Comparison'\n870\t    columns:\n871\t    - Strategy\n872\t    - F1\n873\t    - P\n874\t    - R\n875\t    - Conflicts(%)\n876\t    - Δ vs Single\n877\t    rows:\n878\t    - - Single-pass\n879\t      - 0.445\n880\t      - 0.563\n881\t      - 0.368\n882\t      - 0%\n883\t      - —\n884\t    - - v1 (naive merge)\n885\t      - 0.251\n886\t      - 0.21\n887\t      - 0.314\n888\t      - 28%\n889\t      - '-0.194'\n890\t    - - v2 confidence\n891\t      - 0.298\n892\t      - 0.262\n893\t      - 0.345\n894\t      - 19%\n895\t      - '-0.147'\n896\t    - - v2 priority\n897\t      - 0.285\n898\t      - 0.248\n899\t      - 0.335\n900\t      - 22%\n901\t      - '-0.160'\n902\t    - - Random batch\n903\t      - 0.32\n904\t      - 0.249\n905\t      - 0.446\n906\t      - 31%\n907\t      - '-0.125'\n908\t  figures_description:\n909\t  - 'Bar chart: v1 → v2 confidence → v2 priority → single-pass，逐步improvement但都无法close\n910\t    gap'\n911\t  - 'Merge conflict resolution accuracy: confidence选对率仅58%，priority选对率55%（几乎random）'\n912\t  - 'Precision decomposition: 哪些precision loss来自merge conflict vs cross-type context\n913\t    loss'\n914\t  analysis: 'SDGD v2在worst tier下确认merge amplification是fundamental且不可通过post-hoc merge策略解决。\n915\t    Improvement over v1仅+3.4-4.7pp，仍远低于single-pass和random batch。 关键发现：merge conflict只占precision\n916\t    loss的约40%，剩余60%来自cross-type context loss （模型在无法看到其他candidate types时做出的标注质量inherently\n917\t    lower）。 这意味着即使有perfect merge oracle（0% conflict），decomposition F1仍然≈0.35，低于single-pass。\n918\t\n919\t    对论文的影响：彻底放弃SDGD作为method contribution。 Worst tier narrative下，SDGD全系列(zero/cal/v2)的failure成为paper的重要negative\n920\t    contribution： \"decompose-and-merge paradigm faces two independent bottlenecks\n921\t    —  (1) inadequate confusability proxies, (2) structural precision loss from decomposition\n922\t    —  and solving either alone is insufficient.\"'\n923\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01P4BXChci23qFpkMsGSnMGk","session_id":"a149a487-31d1-4670-8142-477477103f8e","uuid":"9122dd83-0466-4f56-9331-edfec85da88f","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:53:05.550Z"}
